{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers","id":1044917,"title":"Using Sorcerers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-06T22:38:19-08:00","id":1044917,"title":"Using Sorcerers","content":"I was wondering what was the most abusive use of Sorcerer Paths (Mythic Numina, Psychic Numina, or Technological Numina) you have ever witnessed in a game? In my own case, I think it was when a Sorcerer used a Conjuration 5 hung spell (with forty successes from a tenfold extended spell) to send a group of five Mages five miles deep into the sea. In case you were wondering, she had Ability Aptitude (Occult), Mana 5, and five assistants with lesser levels of Conjuration helping her. It was quite impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T00:13:45-08:00","id":1044945,"title":"","content":"RAW sorcerers sound really problematic. If I include sorcerers in a Mage game they are either low-powered, or infernalists--channeling power they have no real control over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T02:04:09-08:00","id":1044965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1044945#post1044945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">RAW sorcerers sound really problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not...really...<br /> <br /> Understand, the above situation is a massive outlier, as Sorcery goes. First, it requires mastery of a Path, which is only really doable for a either a Master Sorcerer, or a starter character that blew all their starting dots on one Path. Second, the character is obviously min-maxed to hell. The Ability Aptitude merit, Mana 5, and as many assistants as possible who are also trained in that Path.<br /> <br /> Add to it that the character only accomplished that impressive feat through ten consecutive rolls, for forty successes. By the standards of successes a godlike feat, sure, but a Mage could probably do the same thing with fewer successes. And that casting probably took a Ritual the better part of a day long. Had to be really lucky that kind of extended roll didn't result in a botch.<br /> <br /> At its core, though, it's not a spell the Sorcerer could just cast on a whim. And it's not really all that impressive, compared to what Mages can do. Overpowered, they are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T04:06:11-08:00","id":1044984,"title":"","content":"Level 3 Alchemy gives you an unbreakable -1 difficulty sword which does +2 damage, level 2 hellfire gives +3 damage and makes the sword Aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T04:09:05-08:00","id":1044985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1044984#post1044984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Level 3 Alchemy gives you an unbreakable -1 difficulty sword which does +2 damage, level 2 hellfire gives +3 damage and makes the sword Aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is still going to be outmatched by a gun.<br /> <br /> Add prime 2 and you get agg damage whenever you like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T05:18:22-08:00","id":1045000,"title":"","content":"Forces 3 and you can even make it hit harder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T06:27:53-08:00","id":1045023,"title":"","content":"The only issue I have with Sorcerers are thier Countermagic compared to a Mage. Simple fix I use is when a Sorcerer is countering True Magick it requires 2 successes for each success countered. End of problem. Incidentally I use the same rule for other supernaturals countering True Magick as well (when I allow it which isn't often).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T07:21:40-08:00","id":1045047,"title":"","content":"I do not find it to be a problem myself, as I think that it encourages Mage players to be careful and to not depend of True Magick for everything. Sorcerers cannot counterspell guns and, especially in the USA, you can get a gun without trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:08:07-08:00","id":1045228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1044985#post1044985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is still going to be outmatched by a gun.<br /> <br /> Add prime 2 and you get agg damage whenever you like.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can quite easily do Strength + 7 (+2 for being a sword, +3 from Alchemy 3 alloy, +2 from ritual) Aggravated Damage with your sword. A handgun does 4 dice of lethal (or sometimes bashing) damage. And the gun example is disingenuous; the Alchemist can make +3 damage bullets, almost doubling the effectiveness of a handgun.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, Prime 2. However, you're forgetting the number of hoops Mages have to jump through. Most Mage Players read off the sphere effects and think that's a list of powers they possess. No. Before Consensus, before Arete, before levels in Spheres, the biggest limitation on a Mage is Paradigm. Most Mage Players, from what I have seen on these forums (and others) simply choose a Sphere effect, and then work backwards, paying lip service to their paradigm. Yes, someone with Forces 2 can perform Aggravated damage with any object they like, however this can be Vulgar, and it won't always fit with your Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Also, our Sorcerer friend can spend Mana with that sword... for 2 points of Mana you can reduce the difficulty to hit from 5 to 3 (the minimum) and now you're getting on average ~70% of your dice as successes. A Mage with only Alchemy 3 and Hellfire 2 (and those only, plus Mana 5 which only costs 5 freebies) with a good setup for using Swords can do an awful amount of damage with absolutely no risk of Paradox.<br /> <br /> Am I claiming that Sorcerers &gt; Mages? No. However, I am saying that Sorcerers suffer from fewer consequences and oddly enough are more free. Their Magic IS reality. Reality is, oddly enough, kind of on their side. Truth Without Paradox. The upper limit for Mage Power is much higher, naturally, but in terms of PCs (who are limited to Arete 3 and take a long time to advance), Sorcerers can quite easily trump Mages at character generation, and if they are clever and played well they can mop the floor with Mages. No problems with Consensus, or Paradox, and their &quot;Paradigms&quot; are meant to be aesthetic, they aren't mechanically restrictive. They also only ever need one Tool/Focus, Mages need many, and a Sorcerer's tool could quite simply be a Mantra or a style of Martial Art or an ancient language, something they can pull out whenever they need it.<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that RAW, Fate 5 can completely screw over almost anyone before they even have a chance to detect it or use counter-magic (I believe that only Entropy 1 would sense this coming, and you'd need decent Arete to get enough successes to see a curse with many successes coming, but correct me if I'm wrong)... but I'll leave that out since I don't let PCs use Cursing/Blessing as it feels like it breaks the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-07-2017, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:13:22-08:00","id":1045232,"title":"","content":"Choosing an effect and working backwards to figure out how it would work in your Paradigm is a time honored tradition. It is one of the really fun parts of Mage and I won't hear a word said against it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:14:17-08:00","id":1045233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045232#post1045232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Choosing an effect and working backwards to figure out how it would work in your Paradigm is a time honored tradition. It is one of the really fun parts of Mage and I won't hear a word said against it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, of course my Meditative Buddhist Paradigm allows for melting people's faces with heat vision! Don't be silly, Storyteller! I... meditate at him. Very hard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:17:29-08:00","id":1045236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045023#post1045023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only issue I have with Sorcerers are thier Countermagic compared to a Mage. Simple fix I use is when a Sorcerer is countering True Magick it requires 2 successes for each success countered. End of problem. Incidentally I use the same rule for other supernaturals countering True Magick as well (when I allow it which isn't often).</div> </div> </div> </div>When you try and Alter Reality at a person whose magic IS Reality, and their Countermagic is Supah Effective, I feel that makes perfect sense. Sorcerers use Magic which is part and parcel of The World As It Is And Should Be, and so I don't shed any tears for Mages who think they Counter too effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:29:25-08:00","id":1045242,"title":"","content":"Well, there are also Paradigm limits for Sorcerers but, strangely enough, it allows them to focus. If someone to create a Sorcerer who melts faces (Hellfire), they will choose a Paradigm that allows for learning Hellfire (or will create their own Paradigm that allows for Hellfire). Since popular culture probably influences a lot of independent Sorcerers, I would not be surprised if a fair number of independent Sorcerers follow the Aes Sedai Paradigm of the Wheel of Time series, the Harry Dresden Paradigm of the Dresden Files, the Witchcraft Paradigm of the Buffyverse, the Force Paradigm of Star Wars, etc. In essence, any structured and formulaic method of magic could be transformed into a Paradigm for Sorcery.<br /> <br /> So, let us take a look at the Dresden Paradigm (which is strangely closer to Numina than Spheres in cWoD). You have the Seven Laws of Magic, you have the division between Evocation and Thaumaturgy, etc. How would you run a Sorcerer who was following the Dresden Paradigm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:31:26-08:00","id":1045243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045228#post1045228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you can quite easily do Strength + 7 (+2 for being a sword, +3 from Alchemy 3 alloy, +2 from ritual) Aggravated Damage with your sword. A handgun does 4 dice of lethal (or sometimes bashing) damage. And the gun example is disingenuous; the Alchemist can make +3 damage bullets, almost doubling the effectiveness of a handgun.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, Prime 2. However, you're forgetting the number of hoops Mages have to jump through. Most Mage Players read off the sphere effects and think that's a list of powers they possess. No. Before Consensus, before Arete, before levels in Spheres, the biggest limitation on a Mage is Paradigm. Most Mage Players, from what I have seen on these forums (and others) simply choose a Sphere effect, and then work backwards, paying lip service to their paradigm. Yes, someone with Forces 2 can perform Aggravated damage with any object they like, however this can be Vulgar, and it won't always fit with your Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Also, our Sorcerer friend can spend Mana with that sword... for 2 points of Mana you can reduce the difficulty to hit from 5 to 3 (the minimum) and now you're getting on average ~70% of your dice as successes. A Mage with only Alchemy 3 and Hellfire 2 (and those only, plus Mana 5 which only costs 5 freebies) with a good setup for using Swords can do an awful amount of damage with absolutely no risk of Paradox.<br /> <br /> Am I claiming that Sorcerers &gt; Mages? No. However, I am saying that Sorcerers suffer from fewer consequences and oddly enough are more free. Their Magic IS reality. Reality is, oddly enough, kind of on their side. Truth Without Paradox. The upper limit for Mage Power is much higher, naturally, but in terms of PCs (who are limited to Arete 3 and take a long time to advance), Sorcerers can quite easily trump Mages at character generation, and if they are clever and played well they can mop the floor with Mages. No problems with Consensus, or Paradox, and their &quot;Paradigms&quot; are meant to be aesthetic, they aren't mechanically restrictive. They also only ever need one Tool/Focus, Mages need many, and a Sorcerer's tool could quite simply be a Mantra or a style of Martial Art or an ancient language, something they can pull out whenever they need it.<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that RAW, Fate 5 can completely screw over almost anyone before they even have a chance to detect it or use counter-magic (I believe that only Entropy 1 would sense this coming, and you'd need decent Arete to get enough successes to see a curse with many successes coming, but correct me if I'm wrong)... but I'll leave that out since I don't let PCs use Cursing/Blessing as it feels like it breaks the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate your concern, but there's no need to explain the importance of paradigm for a mage, I assure you I'm quite clued up on this. Also, I do believe you are somewhat exaggerating these &quot;hoops&quot; quite a bit. A lot of these mental gymnastics are usually done when figuring out how the effect works, but after this, they become pretty standard, sometimes even rote.<br /> We could have a chorister simply say a prayer, asking their lord for strength to protect themselves, and boom, Holy Enchanted Gun.<br /> There may be an Etherite who's simply charging their gun with Plasmic energy.<br /> It could even be an Ecstatic who is so in the flow that they can transfer their own personal energy into the gun itself just be kissing it.<br /> <br /> While your sorcerer spends a few hours creating their sword, the mage can whip out their gun and enchant it in mere seconds on the fly.<br /> <br /> Yes, Paradox is a thing, but for most vulgar effects you only get a single point. Backlash isn't going to happen until you accumulate a lot, and even then the effects can be pretty minimal. &quot;3 points backlash, now I have a nosebleed...&quot;<br /> <br /> How's this for a major consequence. It's a goddamned sword! Run up to someone with a gun swinging a sword about, and I guarantee you'll be shot at least twice before you even get in range of striking, even without any spheres being used. After all, Aggravated damage and Lethal damage function identically in how quickly they kill you. And have you tried carrying a sword around in public? You can't conceal those things without a tremendous amount of prepwork, and even then you're more likely to be stopped by the police carting one around than say a gun, especially since small guns are very easily concealed.<br /> <br /> Lastly, Sorcerers are very much paradigm based as well, after all, how can they do magic if they don't believe in their own techniques? You can't get a mystic pagan witch to do magic with testubes and computers anymore than you can get a faith healer to deal with sinister black tomes. They are confined by reality, but they are also confined by their own belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:34:34-08:00","id":1045248,"title":"","content":"Is Meditate About Things the only tool in your toolkit? Normally I would have added more if I was expanding into other Spheres. Not a problem, though, it works either way. I'll assume he's CoX for this example because meditation is very much in keeping with their methods.<br /> <br /> People often assume that the Ecstatics are limited to perception and self-enchancing effects. Actually, when they are able to get past their own perceptions they realize that the normal barriers on their capabilities simply do not apply. Distance is not real, my form is not constant, and I am not separate from those around me. Indeed I can make my own face melt as easily as I can blink. They are in fact the same motion. And since I am not separate from him, I can make his face melt as well. Blink.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it's pretty damn Vulgar, but there's a lot of potential in altered mental states.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:50:44-08:00","id":1045258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes, Prime 2. However, you're forgetting the number of hoops Mages have to jump through. Most Mage Players read off the sphere effects and think that's a list of powers they possess. No. Before Consensus, before Arete, before levels in Spheres, the biggest limitation on a Mage is Paradigm. Most Mage Players, from what I have seen on these forums (and others) simply choose a Sphere effect, and then work backwards, paying lip service to their paradigm. Yes, someone with Forces 2 can perform Aggravated damage with any object they like, however this can be Vulgar, and it won't always fit with your Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerers also have &quot;paradigm issues&quot;. Perhaps more so. For instence, a Sorcerer that uses Alchemy cannot just magicaly give these propieties to an item, the alchemist needs to do a ritual appropiated to the Path in question. <i>Alchemy powers are all rituals,</i> this it's a limitation of some Paths (like Enchanting) (wich might require either using ancient alchemical forging methods, modern methods, or making a potion), which might need special or expensive components like any other ritual . Also, you can't &quot;mix&quot; Paths to invent new powers without doing a ritual<br /> With a mage you may need to do a ritual to craft an alchemicaly special sword to make it do aggravated, or a special salve, or a matter disruptor. But it may not need a ritual, dependant on Paradigm.l.<br /> <br /> So, Paradigm may not be as much of a limitation for Mages as it's for Sorcerers<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I claiming that Sorcerers &gt; Mages? No. However, I am saying that Sorcerers suffer from fewer consequences... </div> </div> </div>This it's true. Because they suffer no Paradox (albeit there are optional rules to disallow the use of Sorcery in presence of unbelievers, which it's rather harsh)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and oddly enough are more free. </div> </div> </div>This is not, you see, because the following is false:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Their &quot;Paradigms&quot; are meant to be aesthetic, they aren't mechanically restrictive. They also only ever need one Tool/Focus, Mages need many, and a Sorcerer's tool could quite simply be a Mantra or a style of Martial Art or an ancient language, something they can pull out whenever they need it. </div> </div> </div>1\u00ba Their Paradigms are as restrictive as for mages, as I argumented<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba &quot;Needing many tools&quot; isn't a thing in mage. You only need the tool that you need for a certain Rote (a wand to cast Llightnining, a forge to do a permanent enhancement to a weapon, an utterance to do the same enhancement, but temporarily this time). Different Rotes may need different tools, according to your Paradigm, but this isn't different from a Sorcerer, who may need to do potions for Alchemy, to forge an Enchanted item with a hammer, and to speak a Mantra for Hellfire.<br /> <br /> In fact, having 7 tools it's a strenght, not a weakness, because a mage may be able to do the same effect with two different tools (if one it's unavaliable, the other isn't).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:52:20-08:00","id":1045259,"title":"","content":"Except you have that level 3 alloy, which is impossibly light and harder than titanium (IIRC), as very easily hidden body armour under your clothing. That's the normal soak of such armour (which would be about 3 dots) plus 3 from it being a magical alloy, giving a Sorcerer with this exact power 6 dots of soak. Since the gun (normal handgun) does 4 dice of damage, balance of probability is that the bullet will do zero damage. See, with any preparation time whatsoever the Sorcerer has a huge advantage.<br /> <br /> As for carrying a sword in public, you have a tonne of natural and mystical options. Sword-Cane. Large bag with easy access. Disguised sheath. Then if you have just 2 dots in Conjuring you can pull a sword out of your sleeve.<br /> <br /> Paradigm is far less limiting for Sorcerers. For a Christian Sorcerer, &quot;God lets me do it&quot; is a perfectly good justification, following the rules, possibly with ridiculous outliers like &quot;summoning up the 7th Prince of Hell to offer up my service&quot;. For a member of the Choir, &quot;I pray&quot; is not carte blanche to use any Sphere effect you wish. Oh, so God turns you into a floating invisible fire-spitting uber-twink of death. Okay. Now, that is acceptable if in character generation it's established that the personal paradigm of this Choir member is that they believe they are God's weapon on earth, making all but the invisibility okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:52:40-08:00","id":1045260,"title":"","content":"Now, beginning Sorcerers can create more powerful effects than beginning Mages and, because they can hang spells without that much difficulty, they can store a couple of surprises if they are willing to suffer the distraction penalty to their mental and social traits. That being said though, they will only have a couple of surprises ready and, when their surprises are done, they have to depend on conventional methods. Of course, a Sorcerer is probably much more willing to use conventional methods that a Mage (or have modified conventional methods ready).<br /> <br /> If we take the example of a firearm, beginning Sorcerers with Alchemy 3 and Enchantment 3 (Equality for All Rules) can make pistols and ammunition that are quite powerful. With Alchemy, they can create perfectly balanced pistols that have -1 difficulty to hit and can create bullets that deal aggravated damage to anything. With Enchantment, they can further modify the pistols to give +4 to Firearms and the bullets to give +4 to Damage. If they have the Mana Background and the Flow of Ki Merit, they may spend Mana to reduce the difficulty of one attack roll by down to '2', which means that they could potentially be rolling 12 successes on a Dexterity plus Firearms roll (since they could have 14 dice with the modified pistol and ammunition). The combination will surprise the heck out of most Mages, who are not expecting to face that sort of thing, and the sorcerer could straight out kill most things with the first shot (the damage would be 18 aggravated damage, if we assume that the Sorcerer is using a .44 Magnum and that the target gets four successes on their Dodge roll, but that would still average 9 health levels of aggravated damage).<br /> <br /> Of course, most Mages probably know Sorcerers with those capabilities (as each Convention, Craft, and Tradition keeps many Sorcerers around as adjunct members), so there is no reason why they could not acquire similar magical items for themselves. While Mages cannot learn Numina for the most part, it does not mean that there is an opposition between Numina and Spheres. It is more of a complimentary relationship, where Sorcerers do the things that can be done within the rules of Reality and Mage do the things that cannot be done within the rules of Reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:57:16-08:00","id":1045269,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> I'm saying that while a Sorcerer will need some metal and some salts and chalk and runes etc. to make their magical alloy, they don't need to justify why they believe they could. The power is part of reality, and if they have Alchemy 3 they are entitled to that effect RAW. Whether they are a Pagan blessing some earth and then refining that earth into metal, a Christian praying for the steel they make to be as strong as God's Arm, a chemist mixing up a new exciting alloy... yes they do need tools in that ritual space, but no, they don't really need to worry about paradigm.<br /> <br /> In Sorcerer paradigms are supposed to be secondary, they're supposed to just be flavour, they're just meant to add to the world and not restrict the powers. In Mage there are entire sidebars devoted to how Paradigm and personal experience/knowledge can completely screw over your attempt to use certain effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T11:58:13-08:00","id":1045271,"title":"","content":"When it comes to Alchemy and Enchantment in Revised, all of the effects are case as rituals, but they are not learned as rituals. The Paths give you all of the required magical knowledge, though you can master a specific formula or procedure to gain a -1 difficulty for 1 freebie point or 1 experience point (and it reduced the time required in the case of Alchemy). The only Numina in Revised that specifically requires separate learned rituals for each effect is Summoning, Binding, and Warding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:20:56-08:00","id":1045289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm saying that while a Sorcerer will need some metal and some salts and chalk and runes etc. to make their magical alloy, they don't need to justify why they believe they could. The power is part of reality, and if they have Alchemy 3 they are entitled to that effect RAW. Whether they are a Pagan blessing some earth and then refining that earth into metal, a Christian praying for the steel they make to be as strong as God's Arm, a chemist mixing up a new exciting alloy... yes they do need tools in that ritual space, but no, they don't really need to worry about paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>This happens because Alchemy it's already set within an &quot;Alchemical Paradigm&quot;. Tell me what Alchemy power would be innapropiate for a Solificalti to do?. What Mana power it's impossible to imitate for a devoted Akashic that studies chi (or a scientist that believes in the holistic power of Quintessence)?<br /> <br /> It's a bit weird to say that Sorcerers are not limited by Paradigm, when their whole Paths seem to be Paradigms of their own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-07-2017, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:27:25-08:00","id":1045295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045269#post1045269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Sorcerer paradigms are supposed to be secondary, they're supposed to just be flavour, they're just meant to add to the world and not restrict the powers. In Mage there are entire sidebars devoted to how Paradigm and personal experience/knowledge can completely screw over your attempt to use certain effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually true. Have you not seen the section dividing Pyschic, Mystic, and Scientific numina? Or the side bar entitled &quot;Models of the Cosmos&quot; on Page 47 of Sorcerer Revised?<br /> <br /> If it was just flavour, there wouldn't be a whole sidebar of rules for combining paradigms:<br /> <br /> Sorcerer Revised pp.48<br /> &quot;Typically, an extraordinary mortal has only one sort of Numina - mythic sorcery, True Faith, exceptional science, psychic powers, etc. However ,in <i>very rare</i> cases, someone might have multiple talents. To represent this, the cost of any disparate talent after the primary one is <i>doubled</i>. For instance, if a player wants to build a character with both psychic phenomena and mythic sorcery, she can do so by spending <i>two</i> Numina dots for each dor of powers in the secondary aptitude...&quot;<br /> <br /> Let's not forget this little nugget under your path of Alchemy (pp64)<br /> &quot;Alchemy, Herbalism or Advanced Cehmistry? So which is it? Well, all three, actually. Depending on the sorcerer and what belief structure she has, she may study any of them or some strange mixture of all three! Alchemy as a path simply represents any number of material transformative skills that result in elixirs useful as potions, salves, or unguents.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;System<br /> Intelligence + Alchemy (alchemical procedures)<br /> Intelligence + Herbalism (Herbalism procedures)<br /> Intelligence + Science (Advanced Chemistry Procedures)&quot;<br /> <br /> From my reading of this, I can intepret that not all things are vailable to all sorcerers. There might be similar things with near identical outcomes, such as the books example of the Alchemist's Dust of Revealing the Unseen, and the Etheric Interference Detection Gas. Both these things serve the same purpose, they reveal that which is not seen, but even then there are some differences, one key one being that the Alchemist has made a dust, while the Etherite Scientist has made a gas.<br /> To add to this, the third example is a technosorcerer's Radioactive Tracking Powder. Again, similar to the dust, but now it's radioactive, which means radiation poisoning may suddenly be a thing.<br /> <br /> Also, there are marked differences in how either sorcerer would approach their craft. One would require a climate controlled lab, while for the other, a simple workbench would do fine. While the Etherite would need an airtight container to seal their gas, the Alchemist would only need a small jar or glass vial.<br /> If you ignore these differences as mere flavour, then how you can justify your proclamation that there are great difficulties between paradigms with Mages which force the mages through &quot;hoops&quot; in order to cast their effects, I have no idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 02-07-2017, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:30:32-08:00","id":1045299,"title":"","content":"<br /> Paradigm it's always about flavor, they're not &quot;meant&quot; to restrict powers (it isn't it's main purpose). They do restrict powers to save the flavor, and if you disregard paradigm with your sorcerer, it's no different than when you do so with a mage. Sure your Mage/Sorcerer might be able to throw fireballs with Karate (the first chanels ki to his fists, and the second doesn't care because the ST hasn't asked because &quot;paradigm doesn't matter&quot;) but it does the same (service or disservice) for the flavor of both. A question not asked it's not a nonexistent question","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-07-2017, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T12:33:04-08:00","id":1045300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045259#post1045259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except you have that level 3 alloy, which is impossibly light and harder than titanium (IIRC), as very easily hidden body armour under your clothing. That's the normal soak of such armour (which would be about 3 dots) plus 3 from it being a magical alloy, giving a Sorcerer with this exact power 6 dots of soak. Since the gun (normal handgun) does 4 dice of damage, balance of probability is that the bullet will do zero damage. See, with any preparation time whatsoever the Sorcerer has a huge advantage.<br /> <br /> As for carrying a sword in public, you have a tonne of natural and mystical options. Sword-Cane. Large bag with easy access. Disguised sheath. Then if you have just 2 dots in Conjuring you can pull a sword out of your sleeve.<br /> <br /> Paradigm is far less limiting for Sorcerers. For a Christian Sorcerer, &amp;quot;God lets me do it&amp;quot; is a perfectly good justification, following the rules, possibly with ridiculous outliers like &amp;quot;summoning up the 7th Prince of Hell to offer up my service&amp;quot;. For a member of the Choir, &amp;quot;I pray&amp;quot; is not carte blanche to use any Sphere effect you wish. Oh, so God turns you into a floating invisible fire-spitting uber-twink of death. Okay. Now, that is acceptable if in character generation it's established that the personal paradigm of this Choir member is that they believe they are God's weapon on earth, making all but the invisibility okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really feel dumb entering a pissing match between Sorcerers and Mage as this is becoming as ridiculous as the All Mage are Prey thread. But for better or worse I posted this anyways.<br /> <br /> With a Life 3 effect from a Etherites Hyper-Organic-Deletion-Raygun all your armor and fancy protection means nothing since pattern ripping is aggravated and bypasses armor as well as most force fields. Its vulgar certainly but using his hypertech weapon (unique focus) the difficulty is only 5 and can be reduced to 4 with 1 quintessence. With a willpower point he can easily expect 3 successes for 6 aggravated. Pretty sure the sorcerer with his alchemy enhanced armor and sword is on the ground in aggony at this point. <br /> <br /> All the prep you are claimimg for a Sorcerer a Mage can do times 10. Its what they excel at, but whats the point? Whatever 1 prepares another can prepare to bypass. <br /> <br /> On any giving day pretty much any Sorcerer or Mage can step out into the street and get plowed over and killed by a bus driven by a mortal. You can't prepare for everything nor are you always prepared. If you are you probably don't leave the house often since you spend so much time on rituals the days over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:52:08-08:00","id":1045359,"title":"","content":"That is true. There really should not be a pissing contest between the two though. Beginning Sorcerers are specialists while Beginning Mages are generalists. That is why every Craft, Convention, and Tradition recruits and trains Sorcerers, to be their specialists while allowing their Mages to remain generalists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T13:55:26-08:00","id":1045362,"title":"","content":"Not trying to make this into a pissing match, just trying to show that Sorcerers have some powerful abilities available to them Paradox-free, which will allow them to &quot;beat&quot; (hate that word to be honest) Mages in some conflicts.<br /> <br /> As for Paradigm, in Sorcerer all it does is affect Fluff and which Ability you roll. Anyone with Alchemy 6 can create a potion which turns them into a potent low-generation Vampire, it's just that a Wizard takes the blood of some Vampires and uses Salts to purify it and makes a deal with a Spirit of Death, while a scientist discovers the scientific factor behind Vitae, refines Mana from it and creates a mixture which will slow his metabolism to the point of unlife and make him a Vampire. Those are the same thing, basically similar ingredients with different tools and differences in fluff, with a different roll.<br /> <br /> Now, look at Mages. Yes, you can torture your Paradigm to let you do Everything The Sphere Says You Can, but it's really not the point. M20 &quot;How do you do that?&quot; repeatedly drives home the concept of Mages being constantly limited by their beliefs, their views, their own opinions on Magic, their paradigm, their abilities (the Amazonian Forces expert can't make Radioactivity no matter how hard she tries, since she doesn't know what Elements are, let alone Radioactivity) and their culture. This is one of the strongest limiting factors on a Mage, along with Consensus and Paradox. Sorcerers don't have to worry about that because their powers simply Are. Whether the Thor-Worshiper thinks that Thor's powers included healing or not, if they even attempt healing they will eventually learn the Path of Healing. Thor, for reference, had powers relating to helping the downtrodden, including healing. Now it goes without saying that a person whose paradigm is based around worship of Thor would be more likely to use Lightning powers in Hellfire than fire, but there really is nothing stopping them from learning to use Fire since that is literally just part of the Reality of the Path of Hellfire.<br /> <br /> A Sorcerer accesses a part of the real world, simply using their Paradigm as a crutch to do so.<br /> <br /> A Mage alters the world, using their Paradigm as the basis for the change.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there is a better way to put that, but you get the gist. It will never really matter whether this Nun believes that she can curse people or not, if she has a dot in Blessings she MUST have a dot in Curses as they are one Path. A Choir-member who believes that her mission is to bring good fortune to the pious can't pull a curse out of her arse, because that's simply not part of her personal Paradigm. It would take a significant shift in her world-view to allow her to do that, and that could happen on-screen during a session and be an interesting RP opportunity. And yes, a Player Character can choose a very permissive Paradigm, and maybe there's something to be said for a system which precisely balances what the Paradigms can and can't do, but I'm assuming that's a MAMMOTH task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-07-2017, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:18:49-08:00","id":1045379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045228#post1045228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you can quite easily do Strength + 7 (+2 for being a sword, +3 from Alchemy 3 alloy, +2 from ritual) Aggravated Damage with your sword. A handgun does 4 dice of lethal (or sometimes bashing) damage. And the gun example is disingenuous; the Alchemist can make +3 damage bullets, almost doubling the effectiveness of a handgun.<br /> <br /> Oh yes, Prime 2. However, you're forgetting the number of hoops Mages have to jump through. Most Mage Players read off the sphere effects and think that's a list of powers they possess. No. Before Consensus, before Arete, before levels in Spheres, the biggest limitation on a Mage is Paradigm. Most Mage Players, from what I have seen on these forums (and others) simply choose a Sphere effect, and then work backwards, paying lip service to their paradigm. Yes, someone with Forces 2 can perform Aggravated damage with any object they like, however this can be Vulgar, and it won't always fit with your Paradigm.<br /> <br /> Also, our Sorcerer friend can spend Mana with that sword... for 2 points of Mana you can reduce the difficulty to hit from 5 to 3 (the minimum) and now you're getting on average ~70% of your dice as successes. A Mage with only Alchemy 3 and Hellfire 2 (and those only, plus Mana 5 which only costs 5 freebies) with a good setup for using Swords can do an awful amount of damage with absolutely no risk of Paradox.<br /> <br /> Am I claiming that Sorcerers &gt; Mages? No. However, I am saying that Sorcerers suffer from fewer consequences and oddly enough are more free. Their Magic IS reality. Reality is, oddly enough, kind of on their side. Truth Without Paradox. The upper limit for Mage Power is much higher, naturally, but in terms of PCs (who are limited to Arete 3 and take a long time to advance), Sorcerers can quite easily trump Mages at character generation, and if they are clever and played well they can mop the floor with Mages. No problems with Consensus, or Paradox, and their &quot;Paradigms&quot; are meant to be aesthetic, they aren't mechanically restrictive. They also only ever need one Tool/Focus, Mages need many, and a Sorcerer's tool could quite simply be a Mantra or a style of Martial Art or an ancient language, something they can pull out whenever they need it.<br /> <br /> Then there's the fact that RAW, Fate 5 can completely screw over almost anyone before they even have a chance to detect it or use counter-magic (I believe that only Entropy 1 would sense this coming, and you'd need decent Arete to get enough successes to see a curse with many successes coming, but correct me if I'm wrong)... but I'll leave that out since I don't let PCs use Cursing/Blessing as it feels like it breaks the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Primium Bullets, Aggravated Damage. Cost? Matter 5 or Requisitions 1-5.<br /> <br /> Targeting Computation, Default firearms/energy weapons diff of 4, + you're treated as having aimed for a number of rounds equal to every success beyond the first. Cost? One dot of Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Hotshoting. Bonus damage to your firearm or energy weapons damage equal to the damage you would otherwise deal on the effect. Cost? Forces 3.<br /> <br /> High Powered rifle. Cost? Requisitions/resources 1-5<br /> <br /> Putting a Primium bullet through a deviant sorcerers head from a mile or more off coincidentally? Priceless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:23:07-08:00","id":1045382,"title":"","content":"You do not even need that much. A mundane sniper rifle will kill a sorcerer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:28:34-08:00","id":1045388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045379#post1045379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primium Bullets, Aggravated Damage. Cost? Matter 5 or Requisitions 1-5.<br /> <br /> Targeting Computation, Default firearms/energy weapons diff of 4, + you're treated as having aimed for a number of rounds equal to every success beyond the first. Cost? One dot of Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Hotshoting. Bonus damage to your firearm or energy weapons damage equal to the damage you would otherwise deal on the effect. Cost? Forces 3.<br /> <br /> High Powered rifle. Cost? Requisitions/resources 1-5<br /> <br /> Putting a Primium bullet through a deviant sorcerers head from a mile or more off coincidentally? Priceless.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this is an honest question, not meant to be sarcastic. Don't the Primium bullets countermagic those other effects? And if not, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:29:10-08:00","id":1045389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045382#post1045382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not even need that much. A mundane sniper rifle will kill a sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, only if you get a good shot. It's only 8 damage after all.<br /> <br /> And... That is a fairly good question. The primium blocks magic effecting it's own pattern so yes, it would probably block Hotshots.<br /> <br /> I hadn't thought of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 02-07-2017, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:37:14-08:00","id":1045398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045389#post1045389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, only if you get a good shot. It's only 8 damage after all.<br /> <br /> And... That is a fairly good question. The primium blocks magic effecting it's own pattern so yes, it would probably block Hotshots.<br /> <br /> I hadn't thought of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, that wonderful moment when your effects start to cancel each other out. Reminds me of the time one of my players put a Mental Block on himself and the rest of his group, then had a lot of trouble trying to set up a telepathic link between them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:51:36-08:00","id":1045408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045379#post1045379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Primium Bullets, Aggravated Damage. Cost? Matter 5 or Requisitions 1-5.<br /> <br /> Targeting Computation, Default firearms/energy weapons diff of 4, + you're treated as having aimed for a number of rounds equal to every success beyond the first. Cost? One dot of Correspondence.<br /> <br /> Hotshoting. Bonus damage to your firearm or energy weapons damage equal to the damage you would otherwise deal on the effect. Cost? Forces 3.<br /> <br /> High Powered rifle. Cost? Requisitions/resources 1-5<br /> <br /> Putting a Primium bullet through a deviant sorcerers head from a mile or more off coincidentally? Priceless.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're describing a Character with Matter 5, Correspondence 1, Forces 3. Must have Arete 5 or higher. With that level of EXP and time, a Sorcerer is going to be very different to what I've described. For starters, your character lacks Mind, so when a Sorcerer decides to have a little chat he Summons you (Summoning level 5) and you simply trot your way over to his house where you are Bound and cannot attack, and are at -(Successes on the roll) to all dice pools without his say-so. There he can force you to perform any task he wishes, or just kill you outright for fun by flooding the warded area with something (if we're a Technosorcerer, some nerve gas would do).<br /> <br /> Is this fair or normal or balanced or likely to happen? No. But neither is your late-game sniper deciding to murder to death a random dude from a few blocks away. Anyone can simply describe a situation where their character &quot;wins&quot; but it's much more valuable to simply state facts rather than contriving situations. A Starting Sorcerer can beat almost any other starting character in Melee combat (Werewolf is a tricky one, the power-gamer in me wants to have a paradigm where silver is a frequent alchemical ingredient and thus works its way into the sword). I can support that with some facts. &quot;I no-scope the dirty Sorcerer&quot; is a meaningless statement however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T14:54:26-08:00","id":1045409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045382#post1045382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do not even need that much. A mundane sniper rifle will kill a sorcerer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. It's an awful lot of damage, but <i>some</i> Sorcerers would survive effortlessly, while most would be dead on impact. The ones who would survive are Alchemists, Enchanters and Shapeshifters of higher level. With Alchemy you can make a daily mix which lets you soak Lethal, with Enchanting you can get a similar effect as a necklace or something (but it would have a significant downside or maintenance cost), with Shape changes you can (at higher levels) make shifts in your form which let you soak more easily (however I don't know if shifts can be permanent and just left there, they might revert naturally, not sure...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:04:09-08:00","id":1045412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045408#post1045408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone can simply describe a situation where their character &quot;wins&quot; but it's much more valuable to simply state facts rather than contriving situations. A Starting Sorcerer can beat almost any other starting character in Melee combat (Werewolf is a tricky one, the power-gamer in me wants to have a paradigm where silver is a frequent alchemical ingredient and thus works its way into the sword).</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, these two sentences have pretty much ruined any integrity your argument may have accumulated up til now.<br /> It just reeks of &quot;It's only contrived when you do it, when I do it, it's &quot;stating facts&quot;&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:16:12-08:00","id":1045415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045408#post1045408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're describing a Character with Matter 5, Correspondence 1, Forces 3. Must have Arete 5 or higher. With that level of EXP and time, a Sorcerer is going to be very different to what I've described. For starters, your character lacks Mind, so when a Sorcerer decides to have a little chat he Summons you (Summoning level 5) and you simply trot your way over to his house where you are Bound and cannot attack, and are at -(Successes on the roll) to all dice pools without his say-so. There he can force you to perform any task he wishes, or just kill you outright for fun by flooding the warded area with something (if we're a Technosorcerer, some nerve gas would do).<br /> <br /> Is this fair or normal or balanced or likely to happen? No. But neither is your late-game sniper deciding to murder to death a random dude from a few blocks away. Anyone can simply describe a situation where their character &amp;quot;wins&amp;quot; but it's much more valuable to simply state facts rather than contriving situations. A Starting Sorcerer can beat almost any other starting character in Melee combat (Werewolf is a tricky one, the power-gamer in me wants to have a paradigm where silver is a frequent alchemical ingredient and thus works its way into the sword). I can support that with some facts. &amp;quot;I no-scope the dirty Sorcerer&amp;quot; is a meaningless statement however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence why I pointed out that the only &quot;late game&quot; effect which is a piece of gear, could be just as easily obtained through requisitions. This is something a starting technocrat could do if built for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:18:32-08:00","id":1045417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045412#post1045412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, these two sentences have pretty much ruined any integrity your argument may have accumulated up til now.<br /> It just reeks of &quot;It's only contrived when you do it, when I do it, it's &quot;stating facts&quot;&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Listing things a starting character can have is okay, contriving a scenario and then playing it out in written form is less okay. Important distinction. &quot;Alchemy 3, Hellfire 2&quot; is stating facts if you list their effects, talking about outcomes in a very presumptuous way is very different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:22:22-08:00","id":1045420,"title":"","content":"Really? I was pretty sure that Requisitions were limited to mission specific items. I doubt that your superiors are going to sign off on that level of hardware against anything less than a major RDE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:22:56-08:00","id":1045422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045408#post1045408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>A Starting Sorcerer can beat almost any other starting character in Melee combat</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you agree, because this seems pretty presumptuous to me.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:27:12-08:00","id":1045427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045422#post1045422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Glad you agree, because this seems pretty presumptuous to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've cut out all of the qualifiers and context, but for the sake of argument...<br /> <br /> Before freebies you have the ability to with a single action and a point of Willpower, have a burning blade which does Strength + 7 (or higher if you get more successes on the &quot;ritual&quot;) Aggravated Damage. After Backgrounds you have Mana 5, and for 3 freebies you have the power to reduce combat difficulties by spending Mana. With a combat-oriented build and two points in Mana Manipulation, you can keep your difficulties at 3 for the entire combat. Burning Blade means that your swordy Vampire is toast, your swordy Mage has some strong powers but isn't specialized into sword-use this way since their magic is more general, Werewolf is going to beat anything to death, Risen/Ghoul/Kinfolk/Hunter/Mortal/Changeling etc. can't stand up to that setup, from my personal knowledge.<br /> <br /> Push it further and really min-max, and you can use Conjuration to have your sword attacking them from distance, arguably doing a better job while keeping yourself out of harms way, but that is risky... however the cost is zero if the sword has been prepared ahead of time, and that's taken for granted since that's the point of the build.<br /> <br /> And keep in mind that I was responding to a post which can be summarized as &quot;Technocracy Wins you silly sorcerer&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:29:27-08:00","id":1045429,"title":"","content":"I disagree that a beginning Sorcerer can beat any other splat. Yes, they can potentially get one attack out at difficulty 2, but they are dead before then because any other combat optimized supernatural creature goes first. Sorcerers are mortal, and they tend to die horribly when they forget that simple lesson.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:32:11-08:00","id":1045432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045429#post1045429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree that a beginning Sorcerer can beat any other splat. Yes, they can potentially get one attack out at difficulty 2, but they are dead before then because any other combat optimized supernatural creature goes first. Sorcerers are mortal, and they tend to die horribly when they forget that simple lesson.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you say the other one goes first, but you're thinking of Vampires, and while a Vampire might win Initiative based on their Celerity, they're going to struggle to fight someone with a fire sword, needing 5 successes to act normally and avoid Rotschrek. Not 100% sure on other Initiative based stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:34:48-08:00","id":1045433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045420#post1045420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I was pretty sure that Requisitions were limited to mission specific items. I doubt that your superiors are going to sign off on that level of hardware against anything less than a major RDE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Requisitions is limited to 'whatever you think you need for the mission and are willing to ask for.' Are you implying that shooting sorcerers in the head is not within the mission parameters for the Technocracy?<br /> <br /> The mission itself is irrelevant. The only thing that's relevant is what your standing with the union is. If your standing is good, the difficulty is average. If it's bad, it's higher than average, if it's VERY good, it's lower than average. They trust that you're requesting these things for a reason. Three successes is sufficient to have anything you need aside from devices. One success is worth five points of devices. And this is above and beyond what they feel is explicitly needed for the mission.<br /> <br /> Secondly, a handful of Primium bullets is not 'major hardware' by any means. It's average anti-mage weaponry. Pretty much anyone they expect to have ANY sort of magical defenses at all gets shot at with Primium.<br /> <br /> The Union does not subscribe to the principle of scrimping and saving and not escalating the conflict. They hit hard, they hit fast. And they try to end the fight before it's begun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:36:05-08:00","id":1045434,"title":"","content":"The way that Sorcerers win against Technocrats is by preparing ahead of time. Conjugation 5 can potentially send 20 5-ton explosive devices to any location within 5 miles and the targets will be unaware of the attack until it occurs. With GPS detonators, they will explode before the targets can respond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:51:25-08:00","id":1045440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045434#post1045434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way that Sorcerers win against Technocrats is by preparing ahead of time. Conjugation 5 can potentially send 20 5-ton explosive devices to any location within 5 miles and the targets will be unaware of the attack until it occurs. With GPS detonators, they will explode before the targets can respond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Technocrats DON'T prepare ahead of time? Needless Paranoia is practically the Technocracies thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:52:34-08:00","id":1045441,"title":"","content":"Yeah TBQH I'm thinking the Technocracy's bases have some kind of innate counter-magic built into their security systems which will at least attempt to stop Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T15:59:29-08:00","id":1045446,"title":"","content":"Of course, but the majority of them will not have countermeasures capable of overcoming the 20 success buffer that eight hours of extended casting will give the Sorcerer. Then again, there is practically no reason for a Sorcerer that capable to be blowing up Union bases, especially since they could retire after a long career of stealing priceless art. Most Sorcerers could care less about the Union, at least until the Union decides to go after them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:14:27-08:00","id":1045454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045427#post1045427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Risen/Ghoul/Kinfolk/Hunter/Mortal/Changeling etc. can't stand up to that setup, from my personal knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that anyone cares about disputing this line, but:<br /> -A Risen is going to take the hit, heal it and eat you.<br /> -Ghouls, Kinfolk, Hunters (against a mortal) will almost certainly lose....maybe. Serpentis 1 or Dominate 1 would still win (and be hilarious)<br /> -You included Mortal in here....for no reason. Of course regular joe is going to get killed going up and magically enhanced combat specialist.<br /> -And that brings me to Changeling. Like always on here, Changelings are really underestimated. Now, without even going into new material. A few dots of Prop will allow the Changeling to control the sword in all manner of ways (Sovereign can command the sword, Wayfare can jump the sword out of the Sorcerer's hand, possibly teleport it to the Changeling). Dragon's Ire adds a bunch of extra dice to combat pools. Naming is completely broken and comes with automatic (completely unblockable) countermagic circles. Banality can also be used as countermagic (I believe reflexively, though I'm not sure). There are a bunch of other options too. Mostly I just want to stick up for Changelings because they get shit on all the time on the forums. They aren't near the victims of the Supernatural world that people make them out to be.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:18:05-08:00","id":1045456,"title":"","content":"And most Sorcerers who are aware of Changeling are going to avoid attacking them because they always have lots of friends willing to avenge their deaths (and they might come back and avenge it themselves in a decade or so if they have sufficient Remembrance).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:42:02-08:00","id":1045481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045454#post1045454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that anyone cares about disputing this line, but:<br /> -A Risen is going to take the hit, heal it and eat you.<br /> -Ghouls, Kinfolk, Hunters (against a mortal) will almost certainly lose....maybe. Serpentis 1 or Dominate 1 would still win (and be hilarious)<br /> -You included Mortal in here....for no reason. Of course regular joe is going to get killed going up and magically enhanced combat specialist.<br /> -And that brings me to Changeling. Like always on here, Changelings are really underestimated. Now, without even going into new material. A few dots of Prop will allow the Changeling to control the sword in all manner of ways (Sovereign can command the sword, Wayfare can jump the sword out of the Sorcerer's hand, possibly teleport it to the Changeling). Dragon's Ire adds a bunch of extra dice to combat pools. Naming is completely broken and comes with automatic (completely unblockable) countermagic circles. Banality can also be used as countermagic (I believe reflexively, though I'm not sure). There are a bunch of other options too. Mostly I just want to stick up for Changelings because they get shit on all the time on the forums. They aren't near the victims of the Supernatural world that people make them out to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's all fair. Really not sure about Mr. Risen, but those others are pretty solid. TBF I'm pretty sure I was just wrong. The point is always intended to be &quot;listen Sorcerers are pretty powerful and can stand up against other beings&quot; but that moderate viewpoint is difficult to defend since there's a slippery slope between &quot;they can stand up&quot; and &quot;they'll almost always lose&quot;. It's simpler to argue for &quot;they would definitely win&quot; to anchor the argument further towards the desired outcome.<br /> <br /> Like I'm annoyed that the general line with Sorcerers is this oddly patronizing approach to them that the books worked hard to try and undermine but no one seemed to get the memo. I feel like there's something fundamentally wrong with the way players (especially Mage players) view Sorcerers by default, and my response to that is probably more hardcore than my actual views.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:52:37-08:00","id":1045492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045481#post1045481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's all fair. Really not sure about Mr. Risen, but those others are pretty solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Risen are pretty resilient with their soaking everything (to my knowledge) and having 10 health levels and being able to spend Pathos (or Angst) to heal up and still come at you in the same turn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045481#post1045481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">TBF I'm pretty sure I was just wrong. The point is always intended to be &quot;listen Sorcerers are pretty powerful and can stand up against other beings&quot; but that moderate viewpoint is difficult to defend since there's a slippery slope between &quot;they can stand up&quot; and &quot;they'll almost always lose&quot;. It's simpler to argue for &quot;they would definitely win&quot; to anchor the argument further towards the desired outcome.<br /> <br /> Like I'm annoyed that the general line with Sorcerers is this oddly patronizing approach to them that the books worked hard to try and undermine but no one seemed to get the memo. I feel like there's something fundamentally wrong with the way players (especially Mage players) view Sorcerers by default, and my response to that is probably more hardcore than my actual views.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can completely understand. This is pretty much the same stance I take when people talk about how easy Changelings are to defeat/kill. It's bothersome to say the least.<br /> <br /> Oh...one more Changeling thing: with only 1 dot of both Prop and Wayfare you can launch a Sorcerer's (or anyone else's) pants (which will include them because that's how pants work) 10-50 feet straight up or 30-150 horizontally (with 2-4 successes). And nobody expects their pants to betray them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T16:57:33-08:00","id":1045495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045481#post1045481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's all fair. Really not sure about Mr. Risen, but those others are pretty solid. TBF I'm pretty sure I was just wrong. The point is always intended to be &quot;listen Sorcerers are pretty powerful and can stand up against other beings&quot; but that moderate viewpoint is difficult to defend since there's a slippery slope between &quot;they can stand up&quot; and &quot;they'll almost always lose&quot;. It's simpler to argue for &quot;they would definitely win&quot; to anchor the argument further towards the desired outcome.<br /> <br /> Like I'm annoyed that the general line with Sorcerers is this oddly patronizing approach to them that the books worked hard to try and undermine but no one seemed to get the memo. I feel like there's something fundamentally wrong with the way players (especially Mage players) view Sorcerers by default, and my response to that is probably more hardcore than my actual views.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can appreciate that. I kinda see the game books as containing all the biases and assumptions as the demographic they write about, so to me it would make sense that Mage books would look down on sorcerers as &quot;not really magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally, my problem with how useful a sorcerer can be amongst mages comes down to a very big point. Sorcerer's are slow and have a long charge up time. Willpower is needed to do anything, and in my games, Willpower is often in short supply. Most sorcerers would be capable of doing maybe 2 big effects a day for a few days before they'd need some time off to recharge, and depending on the threat level, most mages don't have the luxury of time to wait until the grow their powers back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T17:13:47-08:00","id":1045507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045492#post1045492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Risen are pretty resilient with their soaking everything (to my knowledge) and having 10 health levels and being able to spend Pathos (or Angst) to heal up and still come at you in the same turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> I can completely understand. This is pretty much the same stance I take when people talk about how easy Changelings are to defeat/kill. It's bothersome to say the least.<br /> <br /> Oh...one more Changeling thing: with only 1 dot of both Prop and Wayfare you can launch a Sorcerer's (or anyone else's) pants (which will include them because that's how pants work) 10-50 feet straight up or 30-150 horizontally (with 2-4 successes). And nobody expects their pants to betray them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1: Yes, however 10 health levels in one blow isn't going to be a big deal here. With an optimized build you are rolling 10 dice to hit at difficulty 3, and that's ~7 successes. Assuming Risen splits pool and dodges, they might get ~2 successes. So with 5 successes on roll to hit, it's Strength + 7 + 4, so Strength + 11 Aggravated. Now, whether the Mana expenditure covers both the Dexterity and Strength roll (it's one action, the rules say action) is up for debate. If it's true, you roll up to 16 dice against difficulty 3 for damage. If it isn't, another 3 mana (your last 3 points) will get you that, I could rule either way. That's about 12 damage. Their Soak for Aggravated is their Fortitude, which is ranked 1-5 at difficulty 6. Being generous, if they have Fortitude 5 they will soak 2.5 damage on average. So luck is balanced on a blade's edge here. If the Sorcerer spends Willpower on the initial attack that will just about tip things over. If they survive, they will have a horrific wound penalty (if they even have those?) but can't heal since it's Aggravated. This is all assuming the Sorcerer can't take [type of sword they use] as a Secondary Ability, which could add another 5 dice and some specializations which would add double successes from 10s.<br /> <br /> 2: I feel your pain. Like I think Sorcerer vs. Mage could have been a big theme if they'd made Sorcerer its own game-line and had them as mutual antagonists (with the exception of groups which include both), like Werewolves and Vampires.<br /> <br /> 3: That's amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T17:17:37-08:00","id":1045510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045495#post1045495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can appreciate that. I kinda see the game books as containing all the biases and assumptions as the demographic they write about, so to me it would make sense that Mage books would look down on sorcerers as &quot;not really magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> Personally, my problem with how useful a sorcerer can be amongst mages comes down to a very big point. Sorcerer's are slow and have a long charge up time. Willpower is needed to do anything, and in my games, Willpower is often in short supply. Most sorcerers would be capable of doing maybe 2 big effects a day for a few days before they'd need some time off to recharge, and depending on the threat level, most mages don't have the luxury of time to wait until the grow their powers back.</div> </div> </div> </div>Willpower is tricky. While I don't want Willpower-restoring-potions or anything like that, I see Willpower as a mental extension of energy, and simple Meditation rolls can restore it. This can't happen during a session, but whatever a Sorcerer does to recharge they will learn to be good at it.<br /> <br /> As for spending Willpower, remember that you can trade Power for Energy. So if you have Hellfire 3 and activate a Hellfire 2 effect, there's some mechanic to avoid the Willpower cost, can't remember the exact details. This solves the energy problem quite quickly... I think it just ups the difficulty a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T17:28:59-08:00","id":1045514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045510#post1045510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Willpower is tricky. While I don't want Willpower-restoring-potions or anything like that, I see Willpower as a mental extension of energy, and simple Meditation rolls can restore it. This can't happen during a session, but whatever a Sorcerer does to recharge they will learn to be good at it.<br /> <br /> As for spending Willpower, remember that you can trade Power for Energy. So if you have Hellfire 3 and activate a Hellfire 2 effect, there's some mechanic to avoid the Willpower cost, can't remember the exact details. This solves the energy problem quite quickly... I think it just ups the difficulty a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which means Sorcerers become less viable without that specific path, and dots in meditation. That's kinda sucky.<br /> <br /> I don't see sorcerers as combat characters, I see them as sleepers who have their foot in the door of the magic world, or mystics/scientists who have greater ties to sleeper society. They live half in half out, and as such are able to go by with much less notice. They can perform a numbe rif nifty spells in a pinch, but for the most part the Technocracy leaves them alone, anyone searching for Mages via Quintessence sense usually don't spot them, and because they are not privy to superhuman reality bending powers the mages have, so they tend to be more grounded in reality, more focused, with a head clearer than their awakened counterparts.<br /> <br /> While the Mage thinks &quot;I am all powerful, I can do anything!&quot; The Sorcerer thinks &quot;Right... What's the simplest way to get this done?&quot; It's a nobility that comes from a lack of power, and a resourcefulness that comes from using what little power they do wield.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T17:48:19-08:00","id":1045525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045514#post1045514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which means Sorcerers become less viable without that specific path, and dots in meditation. That's kinda sucky.<br /> <br /> I don't see sorcerers as combat characters, I see them as sleepers who have their foot in the door of the magic world, or mystics/scientists who have greater ties to sleeper society. They live half in half out, and as such are able to go by with much less notice. They can perform a numbe rif nifty spells in a pinch, but for the most part the Technocracy leaves them alone, anyone searching for Mages via Quintessence sense usually don't spot them, and because they are not privy to superhuman reality bending powers the mages have, so they tend to be more grounded in reality, more focused, with a head clearer than their awakened counterparts.<br /> <br /> While the Mage thinks &quot;I am all powerful, I can do anything!&quot; The Sorcerer thinks &quot;Right... What's the simplest way to get this done?&quot; It's a nobility that comes from a lack of power, and a resourcefulness that comes from using what little power they do wield.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the power-trading thing is for everyone. If you have Healing 3 and you want to fix a small sniffle, that's going to be free, stuff like that. It applies to everyone, but you could invent a Path of Power Control if you liked, based around economy of Willpower and Mana, but that might be a bit meta ;-)<br /> <br /> Doesn't have to literally be Meditation. Just take the dots in &quot;Meditation&quot; and say &quot;my character's meditation state is to sit in a dark room and listen to jazz&quot;. Using Sorcery is emotionally exhausting, I imagine most Sorcerers will develop SOME form of Meditation even if that's prayer or watching cheesy films with snacks or whatever. It is, however, a 0-5 skill which is different from passively watching a film or praying without purpose.<br /> <br /> And... that's a slightly Mage perspective, it acknowledges the dynamic, but on a Mage's terms. Here's a Sorcerer perspective.<br /> <br /> Bunch of psychos. Like... my powers can turn my fingernails into claws, maybe give me wings at a push. I can sense magic from a mile off and sometimes, if I'm lucky, see what's coming just around the corner. But there are limits. I feel like if you push too far, try to do too much... a screw comes loose. That's what &quot;True MagicK&quot; is. It's not hard to see... you ever met a Mage who isn't at least a bit crazy? These are people who are so full of themselves that they think they can speak for reality. They all know best, naturally, and their views on magic just have to apply to the whole world. Fuck'em. I don't need to be able to bend myself into 15 dimensions to put a Leech down or guide a kid down the right path.<br /> <br /> That's the dynamic I want. Infinite Potential vs. Finite Potential. Hubris vs. Humility. A Wide View vs. A Personal View. Now obviously there will be those on both sides who don't fit these generalizations, Sorcerers who want to be God-Kings, Mages who don't think their Paradigm could ever speak for all other people or that they know they way to Ascension... but it's a nice balance all the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:34:30-08:00","id":1045551,"title":"","content":"I love playing Sorcerers, even more than I love playing Fera, and it is because they are firmly grounded in mortality. Of course, Sorcerer groups can achieve phenomenal synergy. With Alchemy 5 and Mastery of the Formula, I can make a year's supply of a longevity drug that slows aging to one month per year with just three days in the lab. If I work forty three-day weeks every year, I can supply 40 people (including myself) with that drug annually. With just that expertise, I can become popular and wealthy, and my Sorcerer group will provide me with everything I need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T18:40:21-08:00","id":1045553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045427#post1045427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> With a combat-oriented build and two points in Mana Manipulation, you can keep your difficulties at 3 for the entire combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quoting this because I was curious how this works? I didnt find anything in Mana Manipulation 2 that said you could maintain a lowered difficulty throughout an entire scene. You seem more familiar with this then I am, so I'm just trying to understand how this works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045507#post1045507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 1: Yes, however 10 health levels in one blow isn't going to be a big deal here. With an optimized build you are rolling 10 dice to hit at difficulty 3, and that's ~7 successes. Assuming Risen splits pool and dodges, they might get ~2 successes. So with 5 successes on roll to hit, it's Strength + 7 + 4, so Strength + 11 Aggravated. Now, whether the Mana expenditure covers both the Dexterity and Strength roll (it's one action, the rules say action) is up for debate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would never apply this reduced Dif to the damage roll. Damage rolls are the result of the attack roll. They aren't an &quot;action&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045507#post1045507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If it's true, you roll up to 16 dice against difficulty 3 for damage. If it isn't, another 3 mana (your last 3 points) will get you that, I could rule either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't allow Mana expenditure to be able to lower a damage roll difficulty at all. The Merit is pretty clear that is means to enhance skill. Not monkey the system. And this isn't just to argue that a Risen would do better or anything. I just don't think (and wouldn't allow) this is supposed to work that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045507#post1045507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's about 12 damage. Their Soak for Aggravated is their Fortitude, which is ranked 1-5 at difficulty 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Risen soak all kinds of damage with their Stamina + Fortitude (if they have it, most don't). They aren't anywhere near as frail as Vampires. Also, I haven't seen anything from Wr20 on them, so I don't know if or how they'll be updated. From the Risen book though, it doesn't mention any inability to soak damage in the Aggravated damage section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045507#post1045507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If they survive, they will have a horrific wound penalty (if they even have those?) but can't heal since it's Aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Risen can never fall below a 2 dice pool from wound penalties. So they will always have at least 2 dice to work with until they die. And the Psyche can call upon the Shadow to help for extra Shadow Dice (this is in additon to any powers the Shadow actually possesses).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045507#post1045507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is all assuming the Sorcerer can't take [type of sword they use] as a Secondary Ability, which could add another 5 dice and some specializations which would add double successes from 10s.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is this how they've changed secondary abilities in M20? I honestly had a hard enough time navigating the M20 book because of formatting that I don't know much about the specific rules changes they've made. This seems a silly way to go though.<br /> <br /> (this next part isn't meant to be argumentative, I actually find plotting out the math around these things kind of fun): So using your math, I see the Sorcerer should have a 10 dice pool at dif 3 to hit (once, maybe twice). That's 7 successes with a Str+7 Agg sword. And we are assuming said Sorcerer also has a 5 Str? That puts it at 18 dice of damage. Since I don't agree you can reduce the dif on the damage roll, that amounts to an average of 7 damage. Which leaves a Risen still standing to counterattack. (and since you loaded up and min/max Merits, I'm going to give this Risen the Merit (Speeder) that gives them 2 actions/turn forever...oh and they <i>always</i> win initiative). Putting aside the Risen going first according to the Merit, it would now get 2 actions in a row to attack. It attacks with any of the following: either Usury or Outrage or simple grapples the Sorcerer, eliminating the ability to use the sword against it or uses the Disarm maneuver to take the super special sword and them stabs him.<br /> <br /> Now obviously none of this is so straight forward, but I do think you are underestimating Risen. A well built Risen can be nigh unstoppable (basically the same argument you are presenting for Sorcerers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> Hell...go first and Obliviate the magic sword. You are now facing an unarmed human. Proceed with the zombie movie and eat him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045507#post1045507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2: I feel your pain. Like I think Sorcerer vs. Mage could have been a big theme if they'd made Sorcerer its own game-line and had them as mutual antagonists (with the exception of groups which include both), like Werewolves and Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like an interesting setup.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045507#post1045507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 3: That's amazing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Changeling's strength really does lie in being creative with what they have. Hell, with Fae 5 and Sovereign (Command) they could theoretically command magic itself and turn effects back on Sorcerers or Mages. Not something most people expect.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 02-07-2017, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T19:50:49-08:00","id":1045571,"title":"","content":"No, Flow of Ki is only for physical actions. Damage is not an action or else you would have to split dice in combat (soak is also not an action or else you would have to split dice pools to soak multiple sources of damage). And most pants will tear before they lift a human body far (though I do agree that the resulting wedgie would incapacitate anything with a working groin for a few minutes). And Fae effects Glamour, not magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T20:08:58-08:00","id":1045578,"title":"","content":"One thing that's not generally available to Technocrats is the Invulnerable Merit. At 16 Background points it's certainly a whopper, but.... combined with an anti-magic focused build? They're basically untouchable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T20:11:24-08:00","id":1045580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045571#post1045571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And Fae effects Glamour, not magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Changeling, Magick is composed of Glamour, hence why you can countermagic it with Banality. Now you can say you disagree, but I would still rule it that same way.<br /> <br /> Fae 5 covers: &quot;Anything composed of Glamour: cantrips, treasures, dross, etc.&quot;<br /> Those terms have clear/direct correlations in Mage. cantirps are spells/rotes (any casting really), treasures are wonders, dross is tass. I don't see any reason that Magick doesn't fall under Fae 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T20:15:41-08:00","id":1045581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045580#post1045580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Changeling, Magick is composed of Glamour, hence why you can countermagic it with Banality. Now you can say you disagree, but I would still rule it that same way.<br /> <br /> Fae 5 covers: &quot;Anything composed of Glamour: cantrips, treasures, dross, etc.&quot;<br /> Those terms have clear/direct correlations in Mage. cantirps are spells/rotes (any casting really), treasures are wonders, dross is tass. I don't see any reason that Magick doesn't fall under Fae 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because all Glamour might be magick, but all magic is not Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T20:17:38-08:00","id":1045583,"title":"","content":"Magick can only be effected by Glamour (The Book of Lost Dreams, p. 21). If Cantrips could likewise effect Magick, they would have mentioned it in the Mage section of that book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-07T21:59:22-08:00","id":1045612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045583#post1045583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magick can only be effected by Glamour (The Book of Lost Dreams, p. 21). If Cantrips could likewise effect Magick, they would have mentioned it in the Mage section of that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the page reference. First line in the countermagick section: &quot;Kithain magic and True Magick flow fundamentally from the same source.&quot;<br /> Realms cover broad concepts and everything underneath. Fae 5 covers &quot;Anything composed of Glamour: cantrips, treasures, dross, etc.&quot;<br /> Since Magick and cantrips are composed of the same stuff (i.e. Glamour, according to Changeling) it will fall under that category.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045581#post1045581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Mostly because all Glamour might be magick, but all magic is not Glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>All Glamour is not Magick (with a k). True Magick and Kithain magic have the same root source (again, according to Changeling).<br /> <br /> I would 100% agree that in a Mage game this almost certainly doesn't hold true, since I don't think Mage would ever actually say where Magick really comes from (aside from saying the Avatar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T00:15:37-08:00","id":1045638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045553#post1045553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quoting this because I was curious how this works? I didnt find anything in Mana Manipulation 2 that said you could maintain a lowered difficulty throughout an entire scene. You seem more familiar with this then I am, so I'm just trying to understand how this works.<br /> <br /> I personally would never apply this reduced Dif to the damage roll. Damage rolls are the result of the attack roll. They aren't an &amp;quot;action&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Risen soak all kinds of damage with their Stamina + Fortitude (if they have it, most don't). They aren't anywhere near as frail as Vampires. Also, I haven't seen anything from Wr20 on them, so I don't know if or how they'll be updated. From the Risen book though, it doesn't mention any inability to soak damage in the Aggravated damage section.<br /> <br /> <br /> Risen can never fall below a 2 dice pool from wound penalties. So they will always have at least 2 dice to work with until they die. And the Psyche can call upon the Shadow to help for extra Shadow Dice (this is in additon to any powers the Shadow actually possesses).<br /> <br /> Is this how they've changed secondary abilities in M20? I honestly had a hard enough time navigating the M20 book because of formatting that I don't know much about the specific rules changes they've made. This seems a silly way to go though.<br /> <br /> (this next part isn't meant to be argumentative, I actually find plotting out the math around these things kind of fun): So using your math, I see the Sorcerer should have a 10 dice pool at dif 3 to hit (once, maybe twice). That's 7 successes with a Str+7 Agg sword. And we are assuming said Sorcerer also has a 5 Str? That puts it at 18 dice of damage. Since I don't agree you can reduce the dif on the damage roll, that amounts to an average of 7 damage. Which leaves a Risen still standing to counterattack. (and since you loaded up and min/max Merits, I'm going to give this Risen the Merit (Speeder) that gives them 2 actions/turn forever...oh and they <i>always</i> win initiative). Putting aside the Risen going first according to the Merit, it would now get 2 actions in a row to attack. It attacks with any of the following: either Usury or Outrage or simple grapples the Sorcerer, eliminating the ability to use the sword against it or uses the Disarm maneuver to take the super special sword and them stabs him.<br /> <br /> Now obviously none of this is so straight forward, but I do think you are underestimating Risen. A well built Risen can be nigh unstoppable (basically the same argument you are presenting for Sorcerers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> Hell...go first and Obliviate the magic sword. You are now facing an unarmed human. Proceed with the zombie movie and eat him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana Manipulation 2 lets you store Mana in an object short term, the issue as it turns out is that you need level 3 to draw that from the environment. Do that before a session begins and you're golden. However, Mana 2 is still all you need since you can take 2 points of your own mana and infuse 1 point into any consumable object... for a Martial Artist you could have water, some herbal infusion, a leaf... with very little effort/time you can carry a TONNE of mana on your person, and the only limit on consumption is the medium of storage (although a sensible ST might say you can only regain 1 mana per turn regardless of medium). At higher levels of Mana Manipulation crazy stuff starts happening, you can reduce difficulties to cast spells, make the entire area crackle with your resonance and almost make Reality your Co-Caster if you see what I mean.<br /> <br /> I think I read an old writeup for Risen, maybe Revised? They seem to have gotten stronger.<br /> <br /> That's the Secondary Ability system presented in some Storyteller's Guides. I find it more accurately reflects the depth of human experience. So you have Medicine (Knowledge), Oncology (Secondary Knowledge), Pancreatic Cancer (Specialisation of Secondary Knowledge). When you reach 4 or 5 in an ability you get a free dot of Secondary Ability, at 4 and 5 in Secondary you get a spec.<br /> <br /> Considering all the stuff you listed is stuff I've never seen, I'll say we're thinking of different write-ups, but I'm glad Risen got a boost in Wr20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-08-2017, 06:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T06:54:14-08:00","id":1045726,"title":"","content":"With Mana Manipulation 2, you can learn a Ritual that allows you to store your mana in a potion, which requires an action to consume, so you are running into issues of action economy. With Mana Manipulation 3, you can stored one point of your Mana in non-consumable objects (it does not say you get free Mana from the environment). You cannot drain environmental Mana until Mana Manipulation 4, when you can drain Mana from Nodes or people. Mana Manipulation is really only useful for people with the Mana Background, as the Mana Background allows you to generate personal Mana. Since Mana Manipulation requires 1 Willpower per use, you also start running into Willpower economy issues as well as Mana production issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:11:43-08:00","id":1045736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045726#post1045726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With Mana Manipulation 2, you can learn a Ritual that allows you to store your mana in a potion, which requires an action to consume, so you are running into issues of action economy. With Mana Manipulation 3, you can stored one point of your Mana in non-consumable objects (it does not say you get free Mana from the environment). You cannot drain environmental Mana until Mana Manipulation 4, when you can drain Mana from Nodes or people. Mana Manipulation is really only useful for people with the Mana Background, as the Mana Background allows you to generate personal Mana. Since Mana Manipulation requires 1 Willpower per use, you also start running into Willpower economy issues as well as Mana production issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is why reaching Mana Manipulation 5 is key, as it can allow you to cast lower level stuff for free at a higher difficulty. Then you can just use Mana to counter that difficulty boost. Remember that reaching 5 in a Path can be a matter of years, whereas reaching 5 in a Sphere is 2 seekings minimum and can take the entirity of a Chronicle depending on your ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T07:34:33-08:00","id":1045751,"title":"","content":"Sort of bad economics for Mana Manipulation though. Since you only can only get 'free' Mana from nodes and the 'free' Mana only lasts for one turn per success, you are unlikely to ever come out ahead. While the Mana Manipulation 2 Ritual is useful for recharging between scenes, you can only create so many potions and you still have to have the Mana Background. I think Mana Manipulation is a rather weak Numina and I think that it is better to just have a simple recharge for the Mana Background (Meditation or Sex works well for most practitioners).<br /> <br /> When it comes to level 5 Numina, I really cannot think of a worse investment than Mana Manipulation. You could store some extra Mana, yes, but you have spent 35 freebie points to augment a Background when you could spend 1 freebie point on Ability Aptitude (X), which will give you a permanent -2 difficulty and 5 freebie points on Allies, which would give you five assistants to help reduce the difficulty of your magic rolls. I think that there are much better investments of your time and effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:38:55-08:00","id":1045883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045612#post1045612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the page reference. First line in the countermagick section: &amp;quot;Kithain magic and True Magick flow fundamentally from the same source.&amp;quot;<br /> Realms cover broad concepts and everything underneath. Fae 5 covers &amp;quot;Anything composed of Glamour: cantrips, treasures, dross, etc.&amp;quot;<br /> Since Magick and cantrips are composed of the same stuff (i.e. Glamour, according to Changeling) it will fall under that category.<br /> <br /> <br /> All Glamour is not Magick (with a k). True Magick and Kithain magic have the same root source (again, according to Changeling).<br /> <br /> I would 100% agree that in a Mage game this almost certainly doesn't hold true, since I don't think Mage would ever actually say where Magick really comes from (aside from saying the Avatar).</div> </div> </div> </div>Every splat tries to claim True magic as some offshoot of their things. Just like mage does with 'static magic'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T11:55:24-08:00","id":1045893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1045883#post1045883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Every splat tries to claim True magic as some offshoot of their things. Just like mage does with 'static magic'</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's all that really matters here. This is literally: how does Changeling (the game) view True Magick in respect to how Changeling(the game)'s powers work. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T14:48:50-08:00","id":1046012,"title":"","content":"I would think that the explanation of each splat for their own powers would be accurate and their explanations for other splats would be inaccurate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T15:11:17-08:00","id":1046018,"title":"","content":"Except that this section isn't presented as in character fluff. This is specifically from the crossover section. <br /> <br /> In Channeling (the game), Kithain magic and True Magick have the same source and thus composed of the same stuff. <br /> Fae 5 allows a Changeling to cast cantrips that can directly affect that &quot;stuff&quot;. That's the end of my argument. This has nothing to do with the greater WoD cosmologies. Or what either Splat thinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T16:20:13-08:00","id":1046050,"title":"","content":"But the same book only gives one method of countermagic. It does not specify Fae Realm when it talks about countermagic, so Fae Realm is not required or allowed for countermagic. Fae Realm only effect things of the Dreaming, True Magick is not of the Dreaming, regardless of a random sentence that gives no mechanics, because True Magick does not work in the Dreaming. I believe that True Magick and Glamour are two sides of the same coin, but True Magick is a form of shaped Banality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T20:17:33-08:00","id":1046146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1046050#post1046050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But the same book only gives one method of countermagic. It does not specify Fae Realm when it talks about countermagic, so Fae Realm is not required or allowed for countermagic. Fae Realm only effect things of the Dreaming, True Magick is not of the Dreaming, regardless of a random sentence that gives no mechanics, because True Magick does not work in the Dreaming. I believe that True Magick and Glamour are two sides of the same coin, but True Magick is a form of shaped Banality.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you are welcome to make that call at your table. Given the descriptions I see absolutely no reason why True Magick doesn't fall under the banner of Fae 5. Changeling Realms cover just about everything you can ever encounter in just 4 Realms, at one of the 5 levels given.<br /> The Nature Realm covers everything from Wood to Animals to Thunderstorms. Actor literally covers every sentient being ever (Prodigals gets covered under actor or under Fae in various places). Prop covers anything crafted ever, no matter how simple or complex. And Fae only covers Fae creatures (again, and Prodigals sometimes) in the first few levels before it expands into &quot;all related stuff&quot; as the final category.<br /> <br /> And I'm not talking about countermagick here actually. I'm talking about creative uses for Arts and Realms. The Realm/level Fae 5 should cover Magick. Because it covers everything Glamour-related. And in Changeling, Magick is Glamour-<i>related</i> (since they &quot;flow fundamentally from the same source&quot;).<br /> <br /> Hell, level 4 says &quot;or anything else unexplainable but related to the Dreaming.&quot; Magick (again, in Changeling) is in fact related to the Dreaming. The page you referenced above said pretty much that. Further, Fae actually does cover Prodigals (all other supernatural creatures) at times. You use the Fae Realm when using Spirit Link to cover all Prodigals. By that precedent, level 5 then expands to cover their magical/spiritual energies, the same as it does for Changelings. Also in that book, it states that all you need to enter the Umbra is Wayfare 1 and Nature 1, because those are the Arts and Realms that govern Travel and Nature. At levels 3 and 2, they can do so without difficulty because those are the levels that let you open doorways and affect all living organic non sentient materials. <br /> <br /> And most of this is actually kind of moot since sometime this year we'll have a new Changeling book/edition that clarifies (hopefully) this sort of stuff. Having been the first line to have been abandoned there is a lot to update for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-08T21:07:41-08:00","id":1046164,"title":"","content":"That is true, it never even got a Revised version.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:53:54-08:00","id":1046292,"title":"","content":"Had an idea for a Sorcerer PC/NPC<br /> <br /> Sister Joan<br /> <br /> &quot;I can't tell you if dogs go to heaven, but I can tell you that you can see the weight of a man's soul in how he treats dumb beasts&quot;<br /> &quot;I'm here to look after your physical, emotional and spiritual health love. I'm not here to &quot;kick ass&quot;.&quot;<br /> &quot;They call it Magick. With a K. I've come to realise the K represents the trace amounts of Krazy that come with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> A mid-ranking Sorcerer serving the Celestial Choir, her role is three-fold. She is a First Aider for groups of Mages sent on dangerous missions, a psychologist assigned to assist with mental degeneration and a pastoral (and yes, religious) carer. Having been crucial in rescuing several Mages from the edge of becoming Marauders, she is well-respected by those who have heard of her.<br /> <br /> Abandoned in Warsaw in 1983, she grew up in an orphanage. She had a bizarre affinity with animals and was repeatedly punished for beating up bullies roughly twice her size. Precocious and head-strong, she managed to work part-time through a college education and obtain a degree in psychoanalytics. When she joined the Catholic Church as a Lay Nun in 1996 she took up a new name, as is traditional in many orders. Studying first aid with the Red Cross, she volunteered for several dangerous humanitarian missions. One such mission to war-torn Eritrea led to a very strange encounter. Children were being snatched away in the night, from various towns, villages and travelling communities. Upon investigation, she managed to track down a child who had just gone missing (feeling as though she was being guided by some unseen force). The creature holding the boy was a Nightmare come to life. A hideous, almost rotting creature with fangs and inhuman strength. &quot;The child won't have felt a thing&quot; was the mantra she repeated for years following that night she simply wasn't able to save him. With the child dispatched, the creature leaped at her. She would have died that night, had it not been for a miracle. The creature couldn't bear to taste her blood. By some intervention she was anathema to it. Mustering all of her strength, she beat the creature until it stopped moving, and then watched in satisfied horror as it burnt to ashes as the dawn approached.<br /> <br /> From here on, she devoted herself to the faith, becoming a fully devoted Nun and studying religious doctrine. If creatures like that existed, there had to be someone to protect the flock. She learned scripture until she could recite it, and her faith became like a flame in her heart, a flame that she could rain down on the sinful. It wasn't long before her miraculous healing powers drew the attention of a Chorister, and her new life began...<br /> <br /> In terms of the Character Sheet, Joan is a lost Revenant of the Bratovich line, abandoned upon birth (for some unknown reason). She has no clue about this, having always put her abnormal healing and strange abilities down to divine blessing (for some reason she felt compelled not to talk to others about her powers, which included speaking with animals). She has skill in the Path of Hellfire and the Path of Healing primarily, with some minor understanding of Mana Manipulation and Alchemy. She is skilled in First Aid, and combining this with Healing she is a potent 'support character'. Her own Soak abilities and rapid healing factor, along with her grounded sanity (there are benefits to avoiding Magick) mean that she is something of a Constant, a watchman who doesn't need watching. At ST Discretion she may have True Faith, if there are enough points left (and the ST has enough good will).<br /> <br /> Roleplaying Tips: You're Matron, the rest of the group are very, very clever children. Be affectionate and harsh in equal measure, and always watch their backs. Keep an eye on their mental health, you've seen how terrible the Quiet can get. You are angered by foolish use of Magick, and you tend to view Paradox as a fair backlash against idiocy. On some deeper level you are jealous of the flexibility of Magick, but you accept that God has chosen this path for you. You feel blessed for those you've helped, you are haunted by those you didn't manage to save.<br /> <br /> Healing: 3 or higher. May be replaced with True Faith if its M20 healing abilities (an optional benefit) are allowed.<br /> Hellfire: 3 or higher. A last resort.<br /> Alchemy: 1 or higher. Mostly for mixing up actual medicine in a herbalistic style.<br /> Mana Manipulation: 1 or higher. Used for detecting the Supernatural. May be replaced with True Faith if its M20 &quot;sense evil&quot; abilities (an optional benefit) are allowed.<br /> <br /> Focus: Prayer is the core focus of her work. Her powers mostly come from faith and scripture. The only exception is her Herbalism, which is a mixture of arts.<br /> <br /> Animalism 1: Simply allows you to speak with and (within limits) command animals.<br /> Potence 1: You have +1 Strength and can spend 1 Blood for an automatic success on Strength rolls.<br /> <br /> Abilities: High ratings in Academics, Psychiatry, Medicine, First Aid, Herbalism and Occult. Awareness, Athletics, Empathy and other basic skills involved in a Pastoral role are desirable. The &quot;Prayer&quot; ability (meditation by another name) can recharge Mana and Willpower. Some abilities related to Animals, such as Animal Ken and Ride are relevant.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds:<br /> Mana: 5<br /> Whatever best reflects the respect she is afforded for her Pastoral care.<br /> <br /> Merits: Blood Magic. May fuel Sorcery with Blood if she is out of Willpower. Animal Affinity. True Faith 1 (ST Discretion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-09-2017, 10:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T17:52:06-08:00","id":1046550,"title":"","content":"Personally I would say True Magic is the exact opposite of Glamour, rather than being in any way related to it. Fae, and Glamour, comes from being whimsical, full of fuzzy logic and being willing to just not question things in general. Suspend your disbelief.<br /> <br /> True Magic is all about KNOWING, this is exactly how the world works. This is why. Whether that's a technocrat arguing about physics, a Hermetic talking about the celestial spheres, or a Verbena using their blood to do things. They all KNOW exactly how these things work. Mages have significant trouble spending their disbelief because they spend their whole lives Believing so hard it warps reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T18:31:46-08:00","id":1046570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1046550#post1046550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fae, and Glamour, comes from being whimsical, full of fuzzy logic and being willing to just not question things in general. Suspend your disbelief.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not correct.<br /> Here's the definition from the Lexicon:<br /> &quot;<b>Glamour</b> \u2014 The living force of the Dreaming; changeling magic.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the section on Tempers that covers Glamour:<br /> &quot;The stuff of dreams, the magical clay, the energy of awe, the workings of wonder, the breeze that blows the cobwebs of disbelief from our eyes \u2014 Glamour is all these things and more. The ability to live your dreams, to perceive the true and fantastic essence of the world, abides in Glamour.&quot;<br /> <br /> Glamour is not about being whimsical. It is not about not questioning things. Glamour is complicated. It is a concept that represents a lot of different things. But it certainly <i>is</i> magic. If you <i>believe</i> in magic, you are innately less Banal. That's why most (Tradition) Mages have less Banality than normal people. Glamour is <i>the source</i> of magic (and Magick, from the Changeling game [not IC] perspective).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T18:44:53-08:00","id":1046576,"title":"","content":"Well, Glamour is the lifeblood of the Dreaming, it is not the lifeblood of magic. Linear Magic works by exploiting the Fundamental Laws of Reality, Dynamic Magic works by breaking the Fundamental Laws of Reality, and Glamour Magic works by imposing the Dreaming on Reality. Since the Dreaming seems to overlap everything because everything seems to Dreams (even the sleeping spirits of inanimate objects), Changelings are capable of using Glamour Magic everywhere. Conversely, Linear Magic and Dynamic Magic becomes unpredictable and unreliable in the Near and Far Dreaming and stops working in the Deep Dreaming (which is an argument against Linear and Dynamic Magic using Glamour and an argument for Linear and Dynamic Magic being a form of applied Banality). <br /> <br /> Now, I agree that Changelings are cool, I just do not think that they are the bee's knees. Changelings can counter Linear Magic and Dynamic Magic by using Glamour while Changelings can counter Glamour Magic by using Banality (or redirect Glamour Magic with Fae). Since Changelings use an opposing force to counter Glamour Magic, that suggests that they are using an opposing force to counter Linear Magic and Dynamic Magic. Autumn People might be able to redirect Linear Magic and Dynamic Magic by using a Banality control power, but I do not think that Changelings can do so with Glamour Magic. Of course, feel free to do what you want in your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T21:07:58-08:00","id":1046613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1046576#post1046576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, Glamour is the lifeblood of the Dreaming, it is not the lifeblood of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll give this one more try. <br /> <br /> Glamour is the lifeblood of Kithain magic <i>and True Magick</i>, according to the Changeling game. Which is <i>how powers <u>in said game</u> are defined</i>. <br /> <br /> None of the rest of your post has anything to do with that. This has nothing to do with different game line's cosmologies (which is where linear vs dynamic magic comes in).<br /> <br /> According to Changeling, anything related to the Dreaming falls under the Realm Fae 5. True Magick is related to the Dreaming as far as (the game) Changeling is concerned. <br /> <br /> That's where my argument ends. If you have something that disputes either of those 2 (there's only 2 points of logic) statements, I'd love to hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T21:20:06-08:00","id":1046617,"title":"","content":"'Kithain Magic and True Magick flow fundamentally from the same source (The Book of Lost Dreams, p. 21).' That is the quote that your argument is based on, but it does not say that Kithain Magic and True Magick use the same <i>energy</i>. Kithain Magic uses Glamour and True Magick uses Quintessence, but all that means is that Glamour and Quintessence come from the same <i>source </i>(that the Dreaming and Reality are united on some fundamental level), not that Glamour is the lifeblood of True Magick or that Quintessence is the lifeblood of Kithain Magic.<br /> <br /> My position has to do with the established game mechanics in the Book of Lost Dreams. If you want to change the game mechanics to reflect your idea of Changeling (or the Dreaming), that is your choice, but that should be discussed in the Changeling forum instead of the Mage forum since it is an argument for changing Changeling game mechanics. Of course, it does not really matter, as C20 will likely have better clarifications.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T21:40:13-08:00","id":1046620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1046617#post1046617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If you want to change the game mechanics to reflect your idea of Changeling (or the Dreaming), that is your choice, but that should be discussed in the Changeling forum instead of the Mage forum since it is an argument for changing Changeling game mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not changing any game mechanics whatsoever (and in Changeling, Quintessence is a form of Glamour; and Dross=Tass). But like I said, I'm good arguing the point after that last post.<br /> <br /> Besides, I had considered moving this there, but didn't think this tangent would last more than a post or two back and forth. This all started because I dared to say Changelings could affect Magick directly with the right Realm. I'm sorry that concept was so offensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T03:02:22-08:00","id":1046693,"title":"","content":"Had an idea for a Sorcerer antagonist, would work in a Mage, mixed, Hunter or Vampire game.<br /> <br /> Julian Chambers<br /> <br /> Born: 1100 BC<br /> Current Status: Unknown<br /> <br /> Hermetic Sorcerer (Unaffiliated)<br /> <br /> Julian was born into a family of Sorcerers and was schooled in the lower arts from a young age. Using the masculine principles of attraction, repulsion and purity he formed a somewhat hermetic paradigm which could be compared to the will-working of Hermetic Mages (or even the Blood Mages among Vampires). Precocious and powerful, he obtained a significant amount of magical lore by the time he was 23, mastering several Paths. As the years went by he became obsessed with Lichdom, Vampirism and the powers of Wraiths; all of the power in the world wouldn't mean anything if he was a footnote in history. So he captured and studied Vampires and Risen, he spoke (and sometimes dealt) with weaker demons, seeking for a way to extend his life.<br /> <br /> Using a mixture of Alchemical principles he learned to slow his aging to a near-halt, however this wasn't enough. He knew that eventually some force would stop him from imbibing the draft on which he relied. He used the most advanced (and dark) Alchemical rites, slaying his blood relatives and sacrificing a captured Revenant in order to imbibe his blood lineage with some shadow of the Vampire's immortality. This ritual permanently scarred his psyche, however it did permanently quarter his aging process. This wasn't enough, so his efforts became more... extreme. He made deals with Vampires (any Vampire) to take care of rivals, no questions asked, on the condition that he could do with them as he wished. He acquired 5 torporous Cainites, one of whom was an Elder, and experimented with imbibing their blood. Eventually, after many tests he learned how to neutralize the accursed Fascination inherent to their blood, but the experimentation scarred his internal organs leaving him with a permanent reflux problem (which no amount of magic seemed able to fix). Using this draft (and keeping his &quot;equipment&quot; fed on animal blood) he extended his life exponentially, living right through the long night and into modern nights. He has acquired multiple derangements and supernatural flaws over this period, and if the Humanity system is being used he has fallen to level 2.<br /> <br /> Hellfire: 6 (specializing in the masculine force of fire)<br /> Alchemy: 6 (specializing in concoctions relating to health and longevity)<br /> Mana Manipulation: 6 (he has used this to permanently strengthen his magic)<br /> Shadows: 5 (a mixture of Obfuscate and Obtenebration effects)<br /> Conjuring: 5 (focusing on propulsion of visible objects)<br /> Conveyance: 5 (focusing on levitation and teleportation)<br /> <br /> Mana: 10<br /> Blood: 25<br /> Willpower: 10<br /> Disciplines: Potence 1, Fortitude 5<br /> <br /> He has become interested in the Awakening several times, however he fears that the process will rob him of his immortality and kill him. He fails to understand how the Awakening works, and that his previous magics will probably make it impossible. Furthermore, he sees it more as a transformation people choose to undergo, and he views Mages as beings who have performed some trick upon the world. He is paranoid in the extreme, he feels that he has fought too hard for his immortality. Despite all of his power, he is oddly pathetic; he has done very little with his prolonged life and is a case study in existence for existence's sake. His only real devotions are his own survival and his pride. He runs the line between survival and proving his power over others, and tends to choose isolation where possible. Only a serious enmity or a threat to his existence would cause him to become the enemy of any of the Player Characters. He takes his privacy and his &quot;domain&quot; seriously, so another willworker or supernatural existing in close proximity to him (some highly fortified and well-disguised base, he did away with being obvious when he learned it reduced his survivability) would lead to a few cowardly jabs in the night. Remember that while he would want to destroy or chase away a Mage or Vampire or Sorcerer living within the bounds of his domain, he would never directly risk his life, and so he will attack while invisible or far away.<br /> <br /> If separated from Vampire blood for a month he will age at a rate of one year per hour. If separated from his age-slowing concoction the same effect will take place; he has become reliant on both of them. If he is starved of both he will turn to ash in short order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T06:21:06-08:00","id":1046744,"title":"","content":"I think that he is not powerful enough for his age. If we have the example set by the Kindred (who probably should develop more slowly than Sorcerers because of the stasis of Kindred existence), an individual who is over 3100 years old should have 56 extra levels of Paths (62 levels total with 'Equality for All' rules). In addition, I am unsure that anyone who mastered the sixth level of Alchemy would have not become Kindred dozens of centuries ago if he has already transformed himself into a Revenant.<br /> <br /> I would reduce his Mana to '5' and give him the following spread of Mythic Numina: Alchemy 6, Conjuring 5, Conveyance 5, Divination 6, Enchantment 6, Fascination 5, Fortune 6, Oneiromancy 6, Shadowcasting 6, Shapeshifting 6, and Weather Control 5. The process of becoming a Revenant should not have given him access to Fortitude 5 (Revenants have a maximum of level one in Disciplines unless they have a more powerful master and Fortitude 5 would require a 4th generation Kindred master), so I would actually have the study of Kindred just give him a better longevity potion (Level 5), where he aged one week every year rather than one month every year, before he perfected his unaging serum (Level 6) and just avoid the Disciplines and Blood Pool.<br /> <br /> With his age, he would have 36 bonus levels of Attributes. 21 levels would max out normal human attributes but Sorcerers have access to the Legendary Attribute Merit, so I would let him purchase the Legendary Attribute Merits with Attribute levels (they cost the same amount of freebie points). His final Attribute spread would be Strength 6, Dexterity 6, Stamina 6, Charisma 6, Manipulation 6, Appearance 6, Perception 6, Intelligence 6, and Wits 6. Each Attribute would have an associated Legendary Attribute bonus associated with it (double Strength for lifting purposes, double movement with Dexterity, soak any damage with Stamina, etc). He would have three leftover Attribute levels, but I would just transform them into five extra Rituals.<br /> <br /> With his age, he would also have 155 bonus levels of Abilities, which would grant him level 5 in 30 Abilities and a range of values in 10 other Abilities. In any case, he would probably have 11 dice in any combinations of Attributes and Abilities that predate 1800 AD. In addition to everything else, I would also give him 56 extra Freebie Points for further customization to reflect his great age (Ability Aptitude [X] would reflect the proficiency gained in his Abilities due to centuries of practice and Unaging would just reflect his unaging serum). At that point, you have an ancient and potent sorcerer (with an effective age of 45 due to his longevity treatments before he perfected his unaging serum) who is looking forward to an eternity of life as the perfect man.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer would be looking for true immortality without selling his soul (which is why he is not a Ghoul Sorcerer or an Infernal Sorcerer). With his powers, he is capable of killing from a distance without leaving a mark, using Fortune 6 to wither away that targets of his ire without leaving his Sanctum (even major supernatural creatures would have cause to fear that level of Fortune, especially since his curses could potentially activate before they are aware that they have been cursed) or visit people in their dreams to give them messages. He would know that near future almost perfectly and would have blessed himself to a degree that he could avoid suffering death from practically any circumstance (Fortune 6 with dozens of buffer successes would probably be appropriate). He could transform into a dragon to savage his enemies or turn his enemies into ants before stepping on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-10-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:39:23-08:00","id":1046793,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> he's gained Fortitude 5 using Cainite blood and Alchemy; potent blood can increase a Revenant's max Discipline cap. His high blood pool and Mana pool are from experimentation with Mana Manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T08:47:57-08:00","id":1046797,"title":"","content":"Well, it is up to you, but neither of those effects are part of Alcemy 6 or Mana Manipulation 6. You could easily transform yourself into a Revenant or even a Kindred, but the duplication of the effects of anything beyond the strength of 7th generation Kindred blood should be impossible for Alchemy 6. As for Mana Manipulation 6, it only allows for temporary transformations, not permanent transformations.<br /> <br /> With Alchemy 6, you could potentially make yourself an artificial Revenant Ghoul Sorcerer with a virtual 7th generation Kindred domitor. The virtual vitae would be an Alchemy 6 formula. Other than that, you need real Kindred blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:16:16-08:00","id":1046850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1046797#post1046797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it is up to you, but neither of those effects are part of Alcemy 6 or Mana Manipulation 6. You could easily transform yourself into a Revenant or even a Kindred, but the duplication of the effects of anything beyond the strength of 7th generation Kindred blood should be impossible for Alchemy 6. As for Mana Manipulation 6, it only allows for temporary transformations, not permanent transformations.<br /> <br /> With Alchemy 6, you could potentially make yourself an artificial Revenant Ghoul Sorcerer with a virtual 7th generation Kindred domitor. The virtual vitae would be an Alchemy 6 formula. Other than that, you need real Kindred blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're forgetting that Sorcerers can do ANYTHING with Rituals, they just need to find the right method. So there is a potential ritual for basically everything that Magick can do with a snap of your fingers; there's a ritual to tear down the Gauntlet, there's a ritual to create a Fera line, there's a ritual to do anything you like (and the ST/Lore is on board with) if you devote the time, EXP and research into it. And then there's ingredients. Only 50 million souls is enough to tear down The Shroud for example (that's a Necromancy ritual but you get the idea). Shapeshifting 6 and Summoning/Binding/Warding 6 doesn't just make the &quot;Create Fera Line&quot; ritual, it does however give you the ability to learn the ritual over centuries, and the price will be heavy. I'm thinking that the only viable sacrifice to create a new line of Fera would be a significant number of Kinfolk and Fera of different types for example, and the results would be incredibly imperfect on the first, second and maybe third attempts (like the Mock Breeds of Pentex). And you're not going to survive to make a third attempt, since you just killed a huge number of Kinfolk and Fera, and that's a Bad Idea.<br /> <br /> So a Mana Manipulation 6 ritual to increase your Mana pool permanently isn't too crazy. Same with Blood Pool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-10-2017, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T12:10:06-08:00","id":1046876,"title":"","content":"No, I do not think that Sorcerers are capable of using Rituals to do everything that Mages can do because Linear Magic is bounded by Reality while Dynamic Magick defies the boundaries of Reality. Sorcerers especially are incapable of creating effects that are the province of Archmages (such as the creation of Shapeshifters, which would be a minimum of Life 8 [required for creating physical shapeshifters] and Spirit 8 [required to unify the Spiritual and Physical Realms required to create Fera]). In addition, Sorcerers are explicitly forbidden from combining Numina (Sorcerer: Revised, p. 63) and, while they may be able to create hybrid Rituals at the discretion of STs, there is no reason to expect that even level 6 Rituals would be that terribly powerful (the one example of a level 6 Ritual is Revive which, while powerful, is painfully expensive for the effects that it creates)<br /> <br /> Sorcerers cannot create Fera because they could never develop a level 8 Ritual. The creation of Fera is something that could only be done by Gaia, the Supernals, the Celestials, and the occasional extremely ambitious Archmage who is willing to spend a few centuries on the project. In fact, there is nothing really to indicate that Sorcerers are capable of replicating the fifth level of the Spheres permanently, even with level 6 Rituals and level 6 Paths. Of course, Sorcerers could potentially summon entities capable of creating effects beyond that allowed by Numina, but that is more the realm of Numina and more the realm of Spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 02-10-2017, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T12:41:13-08:00","id":1046888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1046876#post1046876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I do not think that Sorcerers are capable of using Rituals to do everything that Mages can do because Linear Magic is bounded by Reality while Dynamic Magick defies the boundaries of Reality. Sorcerers especially are incapable of creating effects that are the province of Archmages (such as the creation of Shapeshifters, which would be a minimum of Life 8 [required for creating physical shapeshifters] and Spirit 8 [required to unify the Spiritual and Physical Realms required to create Fera]). In addition, Sorcerers are explicitly forbidden from combining Numina (Sorcerer: Revised, p. 63) and, while they may be able to create hybrid Rituals at the discretion of STs, there is no reason to expect that even level 6 Rituals would be that terribly powerful (the one example of a level 6 Ritual is Revive which, while powerful, is painfully expensive for the effects that it creates)<br /> <br /> Sorcerers cannot create Fera because they could never develop a level 8 Ritual. The creation of Fera is something that could only be done by Gaia, the Supernals, the Celestials, and the occasional extremely ambitious Archmage who is willing to spend a few centuries on the project. In fact, there is nothing really to indicate that Sorcerers are capable of replicating the fifth level of the Spheres permanently, even with level 6 Rituals and level 6 Paths. Of course, Sorcerers could potentially summon entities capable of creating effects beyond that allowed by Numina, but that is more the realm of Numina and more the realm of Spirits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that they can make Rituals which use aspects of their different Paths, I don't believe that there should be any ABSOLUTE limit on the potential powers of a Sorcerer. The limitations should be time, EXP, knowledge and resources. Set the cost high enough and possible/impossible stops mattering. So it's simple to say that a Summoning/Binding/Warding ritual level 6 could summon up a spiritual being of the highest order, but you could say that the ritual for summoning up The Wyld would be so complex that it would be a chronicle in and of itself. Such characters are NPCs, you don't get PCs with level 6 Paths and 100s of years to kill. Now imagine an NPC who wants to rebalance the Triat, or unbalance it forever. Imagine the hoops they'd need to jump through. The conflict that would create. The potential stories it could lead to. Imagine if the special Macguffin he needs to free the Wyrm from its insanity (or so he says...) is something of special importance to the PCs, who are fighting for Mass Ascension. As always, what matters is whether it suits the story.<br /> <br /> Why not just make them an Archmage? Archmages aren't really... well first of all M20 is very &quot;fuck you&quot; about Archmages. The subtext of the sidebar on them is &quot;Masters of the Art was a mistake, stay away from it&quot; (at least that's how I read it). Can anyone identify with a person who can say &quot;I roll to move The Abyss closer to The Dreaming&quot;, or &quot;I roll to kickstart the evolution of a new form of life&quot;? And if they want something, why can't they just take it? Go Gandalf rather than Wizard God, basically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T15:47:14-08:00","id":1046957,"title":"","content":"Well, I can see why, from a certain point of view, a Sorcerer using a Path at lvl 6 to do something that requires a big ritual even for Augustus Giovanni, that has Necromancy10, or to an Archmaster with Archspheres (to be fair, Archspheres were supposed to be trated not as &quot;powers&quot; but as &quot;stories&quot;, that's more than rolling to move the Abyss closer to the Dreaming, albeit this was explained pretty bad in MotA), seems needlessly OP. I can even see arguments to that: Sorcerer wasn't a book about how sorecerers can do anything, the biggest ritual of the path of Heal it's a minnor resurrection that pales in comparison to True magick. Alchemy it's the only Path that MAY do something above Sphere 5, and that's a big MAY (it's at the ST discretion). And since at this point we're entering in the territory of ST discretion, it a valid point of view.<br /> <br /> I also can see, however, from a purely Mage perspective, Sorcery being able to do almost anything in time. After all, Mage Spheres opperated with a system that went from lvl 1 to lvl 6 during the whole 2nd edition (and, functionally, less, as Satyros never liked Spheres above 5)<br /> <br /> The whole point of the Ascencion War and the Mass Ascencion it's to make all magick Coincidental. And Coincidental magick it's Static Magick in many books. In a sense you could say that when everyone it's Awakened, the line between Static and Dynamic Magick will blur. However, it's also said that Static Magick follows the lines of the Mythic Threads, that are special loopholes in Reality, they don't bend nor break the rules of Reality, they follow it. Then what if Reality wasn't coded in a way that allows the creation of new Fera if you aren't a Celestine, what if what you wan't to do isn't coded yet?, doesn't the idea of following the rules of Reality looses it's appeal if you can &quot;do anything overtime&quot;?. Reducing the difference between Static and Dynamic magic to one being somewhat slower than the other doesn't feel right to me.<br /> <br /> I like the Idea (that's present in Sorcerer, albeit IOC, and in M20 when they talk about Mythic Threads) that True Mages somehow pave the way for Sorcery to be done. After a legion of True Mages managed to teach that old dog that it's Reality a new trick (like using Hermetism to cast fireballs, or Alchemy to create the Pilosopher Stone), and that trick was instaurated into the collective subcoscious, a new Mythic Thread it's created, an trough will a Sorcerer can learn a way to do it. To me, that's the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-10-2017, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T19:37:46-08:00","id":1047026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1046957#post1046957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like the Idea (that's present in Sorcerer, albeit IOC, and in M20 when they talk about Mythic Threads) that True Mages somehow pave the way for Sorcery to be done. After a legion of True Mages managed to teach that old dog that it's Reality a new trick (like using Hermetism to cast fireballs, or Alchemy to create the Pilosopher Stone), and that trick was instaurated into the collective subcoscious, a new Mythic Thread it's created, an trough will a Sorcerer can learn a way to do it. To me, that's the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would personally disagree with that honestly, considering the fact that there are non-mage forms of magic from other creatures(spirits, vampires, fae, etc.) having mages be responsible fr all static magic doesn't sit right.<br /> <br /> though the thought sorcerery developed from humanity copying the various supernatural races(for this point I'd consider mages separate from &quot;humanity&quot;) is interesting. For example, with all the different shapeshifting magics out there,(mage life rotes, fera innate shifting an gifts, vampire disciplines) it isn't hard to believe that a person or group managed to learn enough of the different tricks accross multiple magics to cobble together their own way of shape changing.<br /> <br /> I also think sorcerer paths are equivalent the same way other splat powers are(a level 3 gift = a level 3 discipline = a level 3 path, except spheres. Mage spheres are weird in that a mage with correspondence 4 could build up 100 successes on a ritual and create a ward that'd stop an antedeluvian)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T20:56:40-08:00","id":1047046,"title":"","content":"I agree, though I would add that Linear Magic should be considered to exploit the fundamental rules of Reality while Dynamic Magick should be considered to break the fundamental rules of Reality (coincidental effects align with Reality while vulgar effects violate Reality). Personally, I like that Sorcerers are not as powerful as other supernatural creatures, and I do not think that Numina should be equal to the powers of the major supernatural creatures because Sorcerers are humans. Numina should probably be around one level less powerful than the powers of other supernatural creatures because humans just do not have the innate capabilities of other supernatural creatures (Changelings have the Dreaming, Fera have the Pact, Kindred have the Blood, etc).<br /> <br /> The fun of playing Sorcerers is that you are humans facing inhuman monsters (whether the inhuman monsters are Changelings, Mages, or Vampires really does not matter). Sorcerers need to depend on the group for survival because no single person in the group can take on even the weakest of supernatural creatures. Instead, groups of Sorcerers tend to be groups of specialists that each give their group a vital edge in the fight against other supernatural creatures (or which give other supernatural creatures a reason to hire Sorcerers).<br /> <br /> I could see a cWoD where Sorcerers end up being the negotiators and the facilitators of the supernatural world. While they are individually less powerful than any major supernatural creature, they have useful powers, they are numerous, and they have human desires and motivations. In some of my campaigns, the members of the local Sorcerer communities managed to unite together to become their own local supernatural factions and, as the average major metropolitan area had hundreds of Sorcerers of each of the three major focuses (Mythic, Psychic, and Technological), they ended up running the local supernatural scene because none of the major supernatural creatures possessed sufficient desire to stop them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T21:51:30-08:00","id":1047055,"title":"","content":"For the little it may count for, I'll preface this by saying that I don't disagree with everything you stated. I agree mostly with the first sentence (on what Linear and Dynamic reality should be).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047046#post1047046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally, I like that Sorcerers are not as powerful as other supernatural creatures, and I do not think that Numina should be equal to the powers of the major supernatural creatures because Sorcerers are humans. Numina should probably be around one level less powerful than the powers of other supernatural creatures because humans just do not have the innate capabilities of other supernatural creatures (Changelings have the Dreaming, Fera have the Pact, Kindred have the Blood, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>So while Sorcerers lack the innate abilities of the other Splats, I don't agree that they're less powerful. In general, the level 5s (and 6s especially) of their Paths tend to be much more power than what most of the &quot;major&quot; Supernaturals have access to. I'd put them above any level 5 Discipline, and above most level 5 Gifts (the &quot;normal&quot; player limits). Mages are the only ones that tend to go above that, but in my (albeit limited) experience Mage players typically don't get to 5s anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047046#post1047046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The fun of playing Sorcerers is that you are humans facing inhuman monsters (whether the inhuman monsters are Changelings, Mages, or Vampires really does not matter). Sorcerers need to depend on the group for survival because no single person in the group can take on even the weakest of supernatural creatures. Instead, groups of Sorcerers tend to be groups of specialists that each give their group a vital edge in the fight against other supernatural creatures (or which give other supernatural creatures a reason to hire Sorcerers).</div> </div> </div> </div>It is worth noting that at this point, you seem to be telling other people how they should be having fun playing a Sorcerer. I certainly don't agree, and I'd wager there are others that don't as well (but would never presume to talk for anyone else). Your view of the WoD seems (from previous threads) to have Sorcerer mercenaries around every corner (or at least in most cities), assisting the &quot;real&quot; Supernatural players (not players as in PCs, but &quot;players&quot; as in the movers and shakers of the Supernatural world).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047046#post1047046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I could see a cWoD where Sorcerers end up being the negotiators and the facilitators of the supernatural world. While they are individually less powerful than any major supernatural creature, they have useful powers, they are numerous, and they have human desires and motivations. In some of my campaigns, the members of the local Sorcerer communities managed to unite together to become their own local supernatural factions and, as the average major metropolitan area had hundreds of Sorcerers of each of the three major focuses (Mythic, Psychic, and Technological), they ended up running the local supernatural scene because none of the major supernatural creatures possessed sufficient desire to stop them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea...your game doesn't seem to reflect the WoD as written in any way, shape or form. If there were as many Sorcerers as you present, then they would be a major force in the WoD. You just said &quot;hundreds of Sorcerers of each of the three major focuses&quot;, meaning at least 600? With numbers like that of even quasi-supernaturals they can and should wipe out the major factions (including Mages) at their whim.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T22:35:34-08:00","id":1047073,"title":"","content":"The majority of Sorcerers are just going to have one level in a Numina. I would suggest that the majority of doctoral-level scientists in cWoD have a minimum of one level of Technological Numina, usually Alchemy (Experimental Chemistry), Divination (Statistical Analysis), Enchantment (Experimental Engineering), Fascination (Applied Psychology), Fortune (Probabilitistic Forecasting), or Healing (Experimental Medicine). When you add them to the people with just one level of Mythic Numina or Psychic Numina, they probably make up a substantial population.<br /> <br /> The characters from Hedge Wizard's Handbook and Sorcerer: Revised are probably the top ten percent of Sorcerers. The problem is that they lack the combat capabilities of major supernatural creatures. Ten sorcerers might be able to take out one Garou, but they would die against a pack of five Garou. Five sorcerers might be able to take out one Kindred, but they would die against five Kindred. Even against Changeling and Mages, they should have a two-to-one numerical advantage to have a chance at success.<br /> <br /> In addition, Mythic Numina and Technological Numina are slow, one turn of casting per level of effect, so Sorcerers cannot depend on them for combat. Yes, Sorcerers can hang one spell without taking too severe of a penalty, but it costs them one point of Willpower to do so. Sorcerers can get one good turn in combat before they end up getting turned into chowder if they forget they are mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T04:10:29-08:00","id":1047148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047073#post1047073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The majority of Sorcerers are just going to have one level in a Numina. I would suggest that the majority of doctoral-level scientists in cWoD have a minimum of one level of Technological Numina, usually Alchemy (Experimental Chemistry), Divination (Statistical Analysis), Enchantment (Experimental Engineering), Fascination (Applied Psychology), Fortune (Probabilitistic Forecasting), or Healing (Experimental Medicine). When you add them to the people with just one level of Mythic Numina or Psychic Numina, they probably make up a substantial population.<br /> <br /> The characters from Hedge Wizard's Handbook and Sorcerer: Revised are probably the top ten percent of Sorcerers. The problem is that they lack the combat capabilities of major supernatural creatures. Ten sorcerers might be able to take out one Garou, but they would die against a pack of five Garou. Five sorcerers might be able to take out one Kindred, but they would die against five Kindred. Even against Changeling and Mages, they should have a two-to-one numerical advantage to have a chance at success.<br /> <br /> In addition, Mythic Numina and Technological Numina are slow, one turn of casting per level of effect, so Sorcerers cannot depend on them for combat. Yes, Sorcerers can hang one spell without taking too severe of a penalty, but it costs them one point of Willpower to do so. Sorcerers can get one good turn in combat before they end up getting turned into chowder if they forget they are mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>The best bet is to use powers which are combat-friendly. Hellfire is 1 turn no matter what level you use. Enchantments and Potions are great; you can get nigh-unbreakable armour which adds 3 to soak, and lets you use your Stamina to soak the damage (unless you take a huge amount of damage and it breaks through the armour). So a Sorcerer with Stamina 5 (great for long rituals) can wear Alchemy 3 derived Armour, and get a soak pool of 8 against most damage (except for things like electricity, poison gas, that sort of thing).<br /> <br /> Get Me The Hell Out Of Here is a great ritual, you can have it resting in the background at all times, ready to take you back to a specific location (as long as it's within range), which can allow for a hasty escape from combat. Plus there are rules for Fast-Casting, so it's not like it's impossible to teleport away using Conveyance (for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T06:53:44-08:00","id":1047184,"title":"","content":"Hellfire is not always 1 turn (Level of effect, meaning casting time, determines maximum damage, range, area, and special effect). Yes, you could potentially cast a level one effect every other turn (one turn to prepare and one turn to fire because you have aim the attack with a Dexterity plus Melee roll), but it would be a horrible waste of Willpower (you have to cast spells as if they were two levels higher, in difficulty and in time, to waive the Willpower cost). Hellfire is much less effective than modern guns unless you prepare ahead of time. <br /> <br /> Alchemy 3 only produces alloys that give one extra die of bashing and lethal soak (I really do not know where you get three extra dice of bashing and lethal soak from) and the unbreakable nature of products from Enchantment 2 does not grant any extra protection to the wearer (though I imagine you could use Enchantment to give extra dice of soak against specific threats). Alchemy 3 could potentially create a potion that would give its user the Legendary Attribute Merit for one scene (which would be able to give the person drinking it the ability to soak any damage), but you are talking about a base of 3 days of preparation and one point of temporary Willpower for one scene of combat effectiveness. If you want a combat Sorcerer, it is much more cost effective to purchase the Legendary Attribute Merit for Stamina during character creation.<br /> <br /> Get Me The Hell Out of Here is a good Ritual, but it takes 10 minutes to cast, so you generally have to hang the spell to have a combat benefit (though you could use it for a jailbreak). Fast-Casting costs an additional point of temporary Willpower and +1 difficulty per turn shaved off the time. Yes, you could potentially teleport away with Conveyance, but you would have to be very skilled or very lucky to achieve a one turn effect for anything beyond 100 feet because you will likely suffer 'traveling while being observed' difficulty penalty during a combat teleport.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that Numina are not cool and I am not saying that Sorcerers are not effective, but you have to modify the basic rules a lot to make them half as combat capable as any major supernatural creature except Mages. Even Changeling (because of Calling the Wyrd and Dragon's Ire) are much more combat effective than Sorcerers, and that is without using their Arts and Realms. Since Sorcerers have superior counterspells, they can potentially be as combat effective as Mages, but they are going to be spending most of their combat casting counterspells against their Mage opponent (and just playing the waiting game until their Mage opponent botches themselves to death).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T08:58:59-08:00","id":1047245,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> Well, a few points. The description of Hellfire states that all effects are Instant. I read that as all spells in Hellfire take 1 turn, you cast it and then aim with Dexterity + Melee (should be Athletics or Occult). So all Hellfire effects take one turn, unless you want to take extra turns to get ready. So a Sorcerer waiting in ambush can spill water on the floor and get a Damage 5, Area 1, Target 1 Shock spell ready, knowing that the water will give it extra Area and they only need to touch the water, letting them spend ALL of their successes on the damage and making it Aggravated. Remember that every Path except Weather Control you get 1 automatic success for your dots in the Path, with the exception of when you fail or botch.<br /> <br /> Also, Mages are highly reliant on Quintessence, and Mana Manipulation can destroy it at a 2 to 1 basis, so in 1-3 turns a Sorcerer can strip a Mage of their Quintessence while keeping up counter-magic. If they're very good they could even absorb it and turn it into Mana, and at level 5 you can add your Mana to counterspells for a Scene, making them very, very magic-resistant. The Sorcerer can block any form of magic which they can perceive, and with Mana Manipulation 2 they can see the movements of magical energies (Magick, Sorcery, Vitae Expenditure, Glamour), so it wouldn't even be that hard.<br /> <br /> So, someone with Mana Manipulation who won imitative against a Mage, had their Mana fully charged and was tactical in their use of Mana, Countermagick and their other skills... I can see them reducing their opponent to a mundane wreck quite quickly. I see a master of magick crying with frustration as the annoying Sorcerer blocks all of their magickal attacks and even their more subtle spells.<br /> <br /> Then a Lupine appears and they're both dead in seconds, so it's all relative.<br /> <br /> For context, all of this would depend on the Sorcerer having Mana Manipulation 5, since that would let them cast level 3 and lower effects for 0 Willpower simply by increasing the difficulty by 1. They'd then have to fast-cast, meaning that level 2 spells would be 3 + 4 + 1+ 1 = difficulty 9. But with a single success they'd have 6 successes, and Mana Manipulation 3 is practically useless anyways so you can ignore those powers. Then you just watch for the flow of magick and actively counter-spell everything, using your own turns to build up a level 5 power which will devote all of your Mana to your counter-magick pool, following up with a level 4 effect to refill from the environment and then another level 4 effect to strip away their Quintessence (if they haven't used it all up).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-11-2017, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T10:44:06-08:00","id":1047311,"title":"","content":"The Duration of Hellfire is Instant because it is an attack, but the Time to Cast is normal (there is nothing in the description of Hellfire that suggests that you get to reduce the Time to Cast and, if you can find such an exception, please share the page number). Mana Manipulation 4 may strip Quintessence from Mages, but it takes four turns to cast the level 4 effect and costs one point of temporary Willpower. Mana Manipulation 5 may increase counterspell, but it takes five turns to cast and costs one point of temporary Willpower. <br /> <br /> Casting without spending Willpower requires an effect two levels higher than the normal level of the effect (Revised, pp. 62-63), so it takes more time and is more difficult. The difficulty for fast-casting an instant level 4 effect (a level 2 effect with no Willpower cost) would be 8 (base 4 plus 4 for the modified effect) and would take an extra point of temporary Willpower and +3 difficulty to reduce the casting time to one turn (the final difficulty would be 9 minus two successes). Fast-casting Numina is rarely effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T13:39:30-08:00","id":1047377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047245#post1047245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>[...]Then you just watch for the flow of magick and actively counter-spell everything, using your own turns to build up a level 5 power which will devote all of your Mana to your counter-magick pool, following up with a level 4 effect to refill from the environment and then another level 4 effect to strip away their Quintessence (if they haven't used it all up).</div> </div> </div> </div>Last I checked a Counterspell requires an action, like a dodge.<br /> Granted, RAW a sorcerer build for it can counter magick like crazy, but your scenario is crazy itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T13:56:50-08:00","id":1047382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047377#post1047377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Last I checked a Counterspell requires an action, like a dodge.<br /> Granted, RAW a sorcerer build for it can counter magick like crazy, but your scenario is crazy itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>From my understanding, Night-folk reflexively roll counter-magick like Soak, not a Dodge. So by the default rules, even the most base Brujah Neonate with Wits 1 and Occult 1, and no clue about magic (just a rough understanding of the basic concepts of the supernatural) rolls 2 dice at difficulty 7 to soak Magick. Sorcerers do the same, but inevitably have high levels of Occult and decent Wits, and can augment this &quot;soak&quot; further with some powers such as Mana Manipulation. Like I'm pretty sure that M20's counter-magick is similar to Soak, not Dodge, but correct me if I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> The Scenarios presented are always dumb. I'm saying that this could happen, not that it would happen or even should happen. If a Sorcerer with Mana Manipulation faces off against most Mages, and wins Initiative, and the dice rolls go their way, there's a possibility that they could simply counter every spell their opponent attempts. But this relies on the Mage getting fewer successes, the Sorcerer succeeding on the Mana Manipulation rolls, the Mage not having any special tricks prepared... you get the idea. But with that said, the Sorcerer can just turn up with a &quot;damage opponent's energy source&quot; spell prepared as a Hung spell, with 20 or so successes in the bag, ready to remove 10 point of Gnosis or Blood or Mana or Quintessence or Glamour from whoever they drop the spell on. Mages rely heavily on Quintessence, so you can see why I'm leaning slightly towards Sorcerers in a 1 vs. 1 (with that said I know that things could go horribly wrong for the Sorcerer, I'm just trying to build the case, I don't necessarily believe that the Sorcerer is innately better equipped or anything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T14:28:18-08:00","id":1047394,"title":"","content":"No, Sorcerer countermagic specifically takes an action (it is a defense, like a dodge, not a resistance, like a soak). And I have never had Mages be dependent on Quintessence in my games because it was difficult to gain Quintessence. In my games, Nodes could generate a maximum of ten points of Quintessence per level per week (Revised, p. 122), which is generous by Revised rules, and unclaimed Nodes were rare (each character could contribute one Background point for a shared Node). My characters thought themselves lucky if they got ten points Quintessence a week. In addition, personal Quintessence (the amount stored by the Avatar) cannot be stolen by magic (Revised, 127-128), so that prepared Quintessence drain attack would be useless against most Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T14:42:14-08:00","id":1047403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047073#post1047073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The majority of Sorcerers are just going to have one level in a Numina. I would suggest that the majority of doctoral-level scientists in cWoD have a minimum of one level of Technological Numina, usually Alchemy (Experimental Chemistry), Divination (Statistical Analysis), Enchantment (Experimental Engineering), Fascination (Applied Psychology), Fortune (Probabilitistic Forecasting), or Healing (Experimental Medicine). When you add them to the people with just one level of Mythic Numina or Psychic Numina, they probably make up a substantial population.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, sorcerers for character creation are given 6 points of numina, so I'd assume that's the average level. Besides, considering how sorcery and numina paths are spread accross splats and how many organizations there are(shih, project x, the arcaneum, supernaturally aware government agencies) I'm sure there are standardized research and study procedures for becoming a sorcerer for those with potential. I'd go so far as to include all types of human numina existing to some extent in each organization as modern conveniences and political alliances mean information and people with information on the supernatural are easier to come by for the people who know where to look, just look at the real life deep web.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T15:14:10-08:00","id":1047419,"title":"","content":"I agree that Sorcerers are less rare than many people think, but there is a difference between dabblers and practitioners. Dabblers are mortals who purchase Numina and Rituals with freebie points, which make them a type of 'lesser sorcerer', which is the type I was talking about (you can find the details in Ascension's Right Hand, Demon Hunter X, Unsung Heroes, etc). Practitioners are given levels of Numina and Rituals, making them a type of 'greater sorcerer', to make them effective characters in crossover games (you can find the details in Hedge Wizards Handbook or Sorcerer: Revised). I think that dabbles are probably much more common than practitioners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T09:06:01-08:00","id":1048264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1047419#post1047419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree that Sorcerers are less rare than many people think, but there is a difference between dabblers and practitioners. Dabblers are mortals who purchase Numina and Rituals with freebie points, which make them a type of 'lesser sorcerer', which is the type I was talking about (you can find the details in Ascension's Right Hand, Demon Hunter X, Unsung Heroes, etc). Practitioners are given levels of Numina and Rituals, making them a type of 'greater sorcerer', to make them effective characters in crossover games (you can find the details in Hedge Wizards Handbook or Sorcerer: Revised). I think that dabbles are probably much more common than practitioners.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think dabblers would be more in line with hunters hunted characters. People who've never considered or looked for the supernatural before finding something that thrusts them into the middle of it. People who are in an organization like the arcaneum would be given access to teachers, materials and the collected research of their colleagues, So I'd imagine they'd pick up the standard 6 dots a creation easily. <br /> <br /> It mostly comes down to if we're talking about joe shmoe who once got attacked by a random neonate and is now hunting vampires with his dad's old shotgun, or john smith a decent agent assigned to the supernatural law and investigation agency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-13T13:03:45-08:00","id":1048395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1044917-using-sorcerers?p=1048264#post1048264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think dabblers would be more in line with hunters hunted characters. People who've never considered or looked for the supernatural before finding something that thrusts them into the middle of it. People who are in an organization like the arcaneum would be given access to teachers, materials and the collected research of their colleagues, So I'd imagine they'd pick up the standard 6 dots a creation easily.<br /> <br /> It mostly comes down to if we're talking about joe shmoe who once got attacked by a random neonate and is now hunting vampires with his dad's old shotgun, or john smith a decent agent assigned to the supernatural law and investigation agency.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love games where Joe and John are both in the Coterie. How do you deal with that? John is a trained marksman, knows how to set up a wire tap or plant bugs, he has a keen sense for danger... Joe on the other hand has some random gift that makes up for him being a bit of an Average Joe. Maybe he has some bizarre resistance to Discipline powers, maybe he has a Vampire Sense, maybe he has a Guardian Spirit or a Psychic Power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}